WEBVTT

1
00:00:49,507 --> 00:00:50,633
It's unbelievable.

2
00:00:50,717 --> 00:00:53,845
I never, ever, let my family
go without anything.

3
00:00:53,928 --> 00:00:57,682
Sometimes I wasn't there because
I couldn't be, but even then,

4
00:00:57,766 --> 00:01:01,478
I made sure everything was taken care of,
so I wasn't missed.

5
00:01:01,561 --> 00:01:03,188
I never even cheated, guys.

6
00:01:03,271 --> 00:01:07,358
Maybe in my mind, but, you know…
But the kids always had everything.

7
00:01:07,442 --> 00:01:09,986
They ask for a lot.
"Dad, I want to take this class."

8
00:01:10,070 --> 00:01:11,821
"I want a drone." "I want a tablet."

9
00:01:11,905 --> 00:01:15,241
I give them what they want.
I keep going. For God's sake.

10
00:01:15,325 --> 00:01:19,245
Then your phone rings.
"It's about a donation."

11
00:01:19,329 --> 00:01:23,041
I don't know what I'm donating.
It's all automatic.

12
00:01:23,124 --> 00:01:26,836
It's important that you understand
that if I'm not a good guy,

13
00:01:27,545 --> 00:01:30,173
if I'm not a good father,

14
00:01:30,256 --> 00:01:34,719
if I'm not a good husband,
then the concept of "good" is wrong.

15
00:01:36,554 --> 00:01:38,056
Oh! Water!

16
00:01:38,973 --> 00:01:42,519
So it's important that you all understand,
in my defense,

17
00:01:42,602 --> 00:01:45,021
that what I'm going through is very hard.

18
00:01:45,105 --> 00:01:48,900
WELCOME

19
00:01:50,068 --> 00:01:55,698
DADDY'S IN TROUBLE

20
00:01:58,701 --> 00:02:02,330
{\an8}2 WEEKS EARLIER…

21
00:02:33,236 --> 00:02:36,030
That's great. That is so great.

22
00:02:36,114 --> 00:02:38,950
{\an8}-Morning, pancake. How are you?
-Morning, honey.

23
00:02:48,835 --> 00:02:51,880
Excuse me, sir, I'm sorry to bother you.

24
00:02:51,963 --> 00:02:54,090
-Keep an eye on the sandwiches.
-Yep.

25
00:02:54,174 --> 00:02:55,633
It's your kids' snack.

26
00:02:55,717 --> 00:02:58,178
Super easy. Green light comes on, ready.

27
00:02:58,261 --> 00:02:59,387
-Okay, honey.
-Okay?

28
00:03:29,584 --> 00:03:33,379
Mom, you're so annoying!
You turn the AC off every day.

29
00:03:33,463 --> 00:03:36,507
-It's so hot.
-Mom, where's my drone?

30
00:03:36,591 --> 00:03:39,802
-I saw it near my closet.
-No. The drone flew away.

31
00:03:39,886 --> 00:03:42,847
Nobody knows where it is.
It's breakfast time.

32
00:03:42,931 --> 00:03:45,099
You're raising your daughter, right?

33
00:03:45,183 --> 00:03:48,228
-Tom Tom is awake.
-Hi, sweetie. Good morning.

34
00:03:48,311 --> 00:03:50,355
Good morning. No good morning for me?

35
00:03:50,438 --> 00:03:51,856
-Morning, Mom.
-Great.

36
00:03:51,940 --> 00:03:55,568
We don't have another thing.
Sandwiches. Daddy let them burn.

37
00:03:56,152 --> 00:03:57,237
Honey, I'm busy.

38
00:03:57,320 --> 00:03:59,989
I can't do everything at once,
for God's sake.

39
00:04:00,073 --> 00:04:03,243
-Mom, we're out of granola.
-Hold on.

40
00:04:03,326 --> 00:04:05,203
The cheese is watery from the fridge.

41
00:04:05,286 --> 00:04:07,497
-Hold on.
-Mom, the butter's too hard.

42
00:04:07,580 --> 00:04:08,414
Hold on.

43
00:04:08,498 --> 00:04:12,210
Since you're my lawyer and you're here,
can you help me with this contract?

44
00:04:12,293 --> 00:04:14,712
I need to get this straight before work.

45
00:04:14,796 --> 00:04:19,550
It's 146, 147, 148. And Clauses 3 and 1.
I'm not understanding the text.

46
00:04:19,634 --> 00:04:21,302
I want to be sharp for work.

47
00:04:21,386 --> 00:04:23,888
-Can you help me with this contract?
-What?

48
00:04:23,972 --> 00:04:27,767
Come on, it's a huge company,
you can ask a lawyer to help you.

49
00:04:27,850 --> 00:04:30,937
Yeah, Vicente could help,
but who needs Vicente

50
00:04:31,020 --> 00:04:33,815
when I have the best lawyer
in town here at home?

51
00:04:33,898 --> 00:04:36,776
-Former lawyer.
-Once a lawyer, always a lawyer.

52
00:04:36,859 --> 00:04:41,197
-There are tricky parts. I think it--
-My dear, let me tell you something.

53
00:04:41,281 --> 00:04:43,616
Every second I'm late,
the traffic gets worse.

54
00:04:43,700 --> 00:04:47,203
If you took the kids to school,
you'd know, but that's not the case.

55
00:04:47,287 --> 00:04:50,248
Let Mommy see, turn around. Look, it's…

56
00:04:51,499 --> 00:04:53,501
-It will improve.
-Found it.

57
00:04:53,584 --> 00:04:55,211
I can't help you right now!

58
00:04:55,295 --> 00:04:57,380
I have to do her hair. God.

59
00:04:57,463 --> 00:05:00,383
-Mommy will try again.
-I won't forget this, okay?

60
00:05:00,466 --> 00:05:02,385
It will be prettier this time.

61
00:05:02,468 --> 00:05:04,262
Let's go! We're late!

62
00:05:04,345 --> 00:05:06,055
-Seriously, not now.
-But…

63
00:05:06,139 --> 00:05:08,516
I can't believe it. Good morning, Simone!

64
00:05:08,599 --> 00:05:11,436
-Mr. Fred is still here?
-He is. Listen.

65
00:05:11,519 --> 00:05:14,314
I went to the market yesterday.
I bought chayote, zucchini…

66
00:05:14,397 --> 00:05:17,567
Sweet potatoes were terrible.
Let's make broccoli rice today?

67
00:05:17,650 --> 00:05:19,485
Let's go, guys!

68
00:05:19,569 --> 00:05:22,030
-Let's go. That's it.
-Good morning!

69
00:05:22,113 --> 00:05:25,867
-Let's go to school. You'll go with João.
-Oh, Tom Tom!

70
00:05:25,950 --> 00:05:28,786
-Bye, Simone.
-I'll take the kids to school. Let's go.

71
00:05:31,414 --> 00:05:35,126
Simone, excuse me. Did you get hurt?
You're limping. What happened?

72
00:05:35,209 --> 00:05:38,629
No, it's just that one of my legs
is shorter than the other.

73
00:05:39,255 --> 00:05:41,591
-Since when?
-Since I was born.

74
00:05:41,674 --> 00:05:44,385
Do you know
what they have at school today?

75
00:05:44,469 --> 00:05:45,845
The day of…

76
00:05:46,346 --> 00:05:49,599
Fred, Simone has been with us
for seven years.

77
00:05:49,682 --> 00:05:53,519
Just so you know.
You missed the limping for seven years.

78
00:05:53,603 --> 00:05:58,024
See? I need your help.
I can't understand this contract.

79
00:05:58,107 --> 00:05:59,901
-Hurry, give it to me.
-Thanks.

80
00:06:02,278 --> 00:06:03,738
Let's go.

81
00:06:03,821 --> 00:06:06,366
-Everyone have their seatbelts on?
-Yeah.

82
00:06:06,449 --> 00:06:08,117
-Let's go.
-Let's go.

83
00:06:08,201 --> 00:06:10,078
Bye, Daddy. Bye.

84
00:06:10,161 --> 00:06:11,996
-Kisses, Daddy.
-Bye.

85
00:06:17,835 --> 00:06:19,045
Let's go.

86
00:06:19,629 --> 00:06:22,256
{\an8}WELCOME!
RABBIT HOME CENTER - ENTRANCE

87
00:06:22,340 --> 00:06:26,219
{\an8}MANAGEMENT

88
00:06:33,434 --> 00:06:34,894
Hey.

89
00:06:38,940 --> 00:06:40,525
Jerk.

90
00:06:41,025 --> 00:06:43,361
Go away. I have nothing to say to you.

91
00:06:46,906 --> 00:06:48,157
In Cambridge?

92
00:06:48,908 --> 00:06:53,246
He speaks English, French,
all at the same time.

93
00:06:53,329 --> 00:06:54,163
Jerk.

94
00:07:00,670 --> 00:07:01,921
-Morning.
-Morning.

95
00:07:13,724 --> 00:07:16,144
-Morning, Mr. Fred.
-Morning, Beth.

96
00:07:16,227 --> 00:07:18,771
The coffee's terrible.
I messed it up today.

97
00:07:18,855 --> 00:07:21,941
Great. You say "good morning,"
and take out the good.

98
00:07:22,024 --> 00:07:24,902
Just drink it fast
because the Board's coming.

99
00:07:24,986 --> 00:07:26,195
That's great.

100
00:07:28,739 --> 00:07:32,368
<i>…don't miss out on our exclusive deals.</i>

101
00:07:32,452 --> 00:07:34,787
These things make me so mad, you know?

102
00:07:34,871 --> 00:07:36,456
We'll deal with it.

103
00:07:39,333 --> 00:07:40,626
Matheus.

104
00:07:52,138 --> 00:07:53,139
{\an8}HUMAN RESOURCES

105
00:07:53,222 --> 00:07:55,892
Of course my toilet can be art.
It depends on…

106
00:07:56,392 --> 00:07:58,060
-Morning, Fred.
-Morning.

107
00:07:59,061 --> 00:08:00,480
-Morning, Mr. Pontes.
-Morning.

108
00:08:00,563 --> 00:08:03,900
Morning, Dante. Glad to see you here.
Everything okay?

109
00:08:03,983 --> 00:08:07,737
Fred, Matheus has
something to show you. Please.

110
00:08:07,820 --> 00:08:11,741
A cleaning staff employee was caught
on the security cameras.

111
00:08:24,462 --> 00:08:25,713
What did she steal?

112
00:08:26,672 --> 00:08:29,509
Wing screws. Three of them.

113
00:08:29,592 --> 00:08:30,968
-Three boxes?
-No.

114
00:08:31,802 --> 00:08:33,888
-Three screws.
-Oh, okay.

115
00:08:34,597 --> 00:08:35,723
I thought…

116
00:08:36,307 --> 00:08:38,809
We have a delicate situation on our hands.

117
00:08:38,893 --> 00:08:42,063
Someone steals,
but they steal three items.

118
00:08:42,647 --> 00:08:45,650
-Yeah.
-What do you do with this person?

119
00:08:47,735 --> 00:08:48,903
What do you do?

120
00:08:50,321 --> 00:08:52,949
Petty theft, nothing major, right?
You can't…

121
00:08:54,075 --> 00:08:58,120
It's complicated. I think, to be fair,
we should issue a warning.

122
00:08:58,204 --> 00:09:00,831
-Yes.
-We make an example of her.

123
00:09:00,915 --> 00:09:04,752
For the company as a whole…

124
00:09:04,835 --> 00:09:06,337
-No?
-Maybe.

125
00:09:06,420 --> 00:09:07,463
What do you mean?

126
00:09:07,547 --> 00:09:10,383
A warning? Today, it's three wing screws,

127
00:09:10,466 --> 00:09:12,426
tomorrow it's an armed robbery.

128
00:09:14,262 --> 00:09:16,305
-Robbery?
-Yes, that's true.

129
00:09:16,389 --> 00:09:17,390
-Is it?
-It is.

130
00:09:17,473 --> 00:09:19,225
It is. No, of course it is.

131
00:09:19,809 --> 00:09:22,603
He's absolutely right.
And we have to lead by example.

132
00:09:22,687 --> 00:09:26,065
We have to lead by example.
Here's what I propose.

133
00:09:26,148 --> 00:09:28,484
A three-day suspension
so she can think about it.

134
00:09:28,568 --> 00:09:30,152
-Sure.
-Right?

135
00:09:30,236 --> 00:09:32,697
Three days. One for each screw.

136
00:09:33,489 --> 00:09:36,325
I feel like you're downplaying
the offense, Fred.

137
00:09:37,326 --> 00:09:38,786
-Maybe.
-Me?

138
00:09:38,869 --> 00:09:41,080
-Yes.
-No…

139
00:09:41,581 --> 00:09:44,166
I actually thought three days per screw.

140
00:09:44,250 --> 00:09:46,919
You didn't let me finish
my train of thought.

141
00:09:48,004 --> 00:09:50,464
Three days for each screw.

142
00:09:50,548 --> 00:09:52,341
So, nine. Let's call it ten.

143
00:09:52,425 --> 00:09:54,385
Yes. Makes sense.

144
00:09:54,468 --> 00:09:55,595
In my opinion,

145
00:09:55,678 --> 00:09:58,764
that lady should pay
for the entire stock of screws.

146
00:09:58,848 --> 00:10:00,016
Hey.

147
00:10:00,099 --> 00:10:01,350
Look.

148
00:10:01,434 --> 00:10:02,685
I agree.

149
00:10:02,768 --> 00:10:05,896
Guys, come on. Enough is enough!

150
00:10:05,980 --> 00:10:09,942
Let's be rational here. 'Cause…
I'm noticing something very common.

151
00:10:10,026 --> 00:10:14,196
Emotion's overtaking reason.
Enough, guys. I say we fire the lady now.

152
00:10:14,280 --> 00:10:18,701
No, I agree. I agree.
We can't let reason be clouded by emotion.

153
00:10:18,784 --> 00:10:22,038
-Exactly.
-Very good. Very good, Fred.

154
00:10:22,121 --> 00:10:25,833
The termination paperwork's here.
Sign it, let's get this done.

155
00:10:30,546 --> 00:10:33,049
I don't have my pen, because I…

156
00:10:33,132 --> 00:10:34,050
Use mine.

157
00:10:36,677 --> 00:10:37,970
Matheus.

158
00:10:39,138 --> 00:10:40,681
-That was heavy.
-What the hell?

159
00:10:40,765 --> 00:10:43,976
-That was unnecessary.
-At least it's two-for-one beers Tuesday.

160
00:10:44,060 --> 00:10:45,728
-Nice.
-I want both.

161
00:10:45,811 --> 00:10:49,273
I'll ask for one, get two,
and drink them, no sharing.

162
00:10:49,357 --> 00:10:51,525
-What? Why so selfish?
-Selfish?

163
00:10:51,609 --> 00:10:54,362
Look what I'm going through,
what Dante does to me.

164
00:10:54,445 --> 00:10:57,990
-He's like a soap opera villain.
-No, Mr. Pontes is--

165
00:10:58,074 --> 00:11:01,410
-He's more of a suck-up.
-So there are two villains.

166
00:11:01,952 --> 00:11:03,579
-Two nuisances in my life.
-Yes.

167
00:11:03,663 --> 00:11:06,457
Jesus. Good thing
it's two-for-one Tuesday,

168
00:11:06,540 --> 00:11:08,918
because we really need and deserve it.

169
00:11:09,001 --> 00:11:11,712
Yeah. You'll go home seeing double.

170
00:11:12,421 --> 00:11:14,632
-To us.
-To our choices.

171
00:11:14,715 --> 00:11:16,509
-And loved ones.
-To loved ones.

172
00:11:16,592 --> 00:11:20,596
Yeah. Thanks, Marconi.
I appreciate it, buddy.

173
00:11:20,680 --> 00:11:23,349
Being an adult sucks, man.

174
00:11:23,432 --> 00:11:25,976
And we thought it would be easier. Right?

175
00:11:26,060 --> 00:11:30,314
Roberta is the lucky one.
She's there smelling them…

176
00:11:30,398 --> 00:11:32,566
You know? That's luck.

177
00:11:33,609 --> 00:11:36,487
Clarice! I already told you to stop that.

178
00:11:36,570 --> 00:11:38,989
Mom, João is breaking our TV deal.

179
00:11:39,073 --> 00:11:42,993
I asked for five minutes, Mom.
Could you stop being so annoying?

180
00:11:44,120 --> 00:11:45,705
-I'm hungry, Mom.
-Me too.

181
00:11:45,788 --> 00:11:47,915
I'm only one person,
taking care of your brother.

182
00:11:47,998 --> 00:11:49,709
-Where's Dad?
-He could bring pizza.

183
00:11:49,792 --> 00:11:53,087
Oh, but today's Tuesday,
and Dad's partying.

184
00:11:53,170 --> 00:11:55,715
He won't be home until ten.

185
00:11:57,591 --> 00:11:59,719
-No.
-Give me the remote, João!

186
00:11:59,802 --> 00:12:01,554
-Give me five minutes!
-Give it to me!

187
00:12:01,637 --> 00:12:04,056
-I'm the oldest.
-You wouldn't give me five minutes.

188
00:12:04,640 --> 00:12:07,143
Speaking of things we're thinking about…

189
00:12:09,395 --> 00:12:12,022
His face is just like yours,
but it's better on him.

190
00:12:23,743 --> 00:12:25,161
10:08 PM

191
00:12:26,537 --> 00:12:27,913
Found it!

192
00:12:30,958 --> 00:12:34,962
-Let's call the kids?
-Stop it, man.

193
00:13:00,446 --> 00:13:03,783
Can I ask who let you stay up this late?

194
00:13:03,866 --> 00:13:05,075
Even Tom Tom's awake.

195
00:13:05,159 --> 00:13:09,038
He just fell asleep, and God help you
if you wake him up. Turn off the TV now.

196
00:13:09,121 --> 00:13:11,791
João's playing the guitar
and you're not saying anything.

197
00:13:11,874 --> 00:13:13,834
Because this scolding is for you.

198
00:13:13,918 --> 00:13:17,630
João's scolding is being prepared
and will come his way soon.

199
00:13:17,713 --> 00:13:19,465
Enough. Stop with the guitar.

200
00:13:19,548 --> 00:13:22,551
God, Mom, can't you see I'm playing?

201
00:13:22,635 --> 00:13:25,262
-I wanted to watch TV!
-I had the remote!

202
00:13:25,346 --> 00:13:27,223
-I wanted!
-If I don't ask for--

203
00:13:27,306 --> 00:13:29,183
Enough!

204
00:13:29,266 --> 00:13:31,352
That's it!

205
00:13:31,435 --> 00:13:33,896
No more zombies! No more guitar!

206
00:13:33,979 --> 00:13:37,066
No more anything!
It's over, it's the Apocalypse!

207
00:13:37,149 --> 00:13:40,736
I'll personally bring the Apocalypse
to this house! Enough!

208
00:13:40,820 --> 00:13:42,279
What's going on, honey?

209
00:13:43,030 --> 00:13:44,824
This isn't the Roberta I know.

210
00:13:44,907 --> 00:13:49,870
Fred, you just witnessed a scene
which is hard to defend myself for.

211
00:13:49,954 --> 00:13:52,414
Mommy's credibility
has taken a bit of a hit.

212
00:13:52,498 --> 00:13:57,419
But if you had seen
the moments that led up to this,

213
00:13:57,503 --> 00:13:58,921
you would understand.

214
00:13:59,004 --> 00:14:00,464
But you didn't.

215
00:14:00,548 --> 00:14:03,217
Because you weren't at home.
You were at the bar.

216
00:14:03,300 --> 00:14:05,553
Living your best life with your bro.

217
00:14:05,636 --> 00:14:07,596
So you didn't see it, right?

218
00:14:07,680 --> 00:14:09,849
-Single mom.
-Honey, the kids.

219
00:14:09,932 --> 00:14:12,268
Kids, go upstairs for a bit,
Mommy wants to talk

220
00:14:12,351 --> 00:14:14,061
to Daddy about grown-up stuff.

221
00:14:14,144 --> 00:14:15,896
Yes, go, Mommy wants to talk to Daddy.

222
00:14:15,980 --> 00:14:19,108
-That was crazy.
-Just go.

223
00:14:20,484 --> 00:14:22,027
Nicely done, huh, Roberta?

224
00:14:22,570 --> 00:14:26,073
You wash your hands of it
and blame it all on the father?

225
00:14:26,156 --> 00:14:28,200
You're the one washing your hands.

226
00:14:28,284 --> 00:14:30,703
-Me?
-You weren't home, you went to the bar.

227
00:14:30,786 --> 00:14:31,871
And vanished.

228
00:14:47,011 --> 00:14:49,555
-Found it!
-Oh, Matheus, thank you.

229
00:14:49,638 --> 00:14:51,682
-I'll throw it!
-Let me tell you.

230
00:14:51,765 --> 00:14:53,517
Everything's wonderful, the barbecue…

231
00:14:53,601 --> 00:14:57,187
But I need your help, everyone's help.
This barbecue needs to save my marriage.

232
00:14:57,271 --> 00:14:59,982
Roberta hasn't looked me
in the eye since Tuesday.

233
00:15:00,065 --> 00:15:03,110
So you got two-for-one beers
and two-for-one scoldings.

234
00:15:03,193 --> 00:15:05,195
I wish it was only two-for-one.

235
00:15:05,279 --> 00:15:09,325
I got five-for-one scoldings, one per kid,
plus one for Roberta.

236
00:15:09,408 --> 00:15:11,493
So things are complicated, rough.

237
00:15:11,577 --> 00:15:13,537
I had an idea. Maybe you could…

238
00:15:13,621 --> 00:15:16,582
When we're eating,
you could talk me up a bit.

239
00:15:16,665 --> 00:15:20,920
Praise me for making the barbecue…
Compliment me a little bit, all right?

240
00:15:21,003 --> 00:15:22,630
-I'll improvise.
-Thanks.

241
00:15:22,713 --> 00:15:24,590
If you forget, I'll give a signal.

242
00:15:24,673 --> 00:15:26,550
-What?
-This is the signal.

243
00:15:26,634 --> 00:15:28,802
-Be more discreet. That's it.
-Okay.

244
00:15:28,886 --> 00:15:33,557
Who came up with the barbecue idea?
I'm so mad I'm about to become a vegan.

245
00:15:33,641 --> 00:15:36,560
For us to meet up.
You needed to see your little sis.

246
00:15:37,144 --> 00:15:39,980
"Little sister."
I loved the "little" part.

247
00:15:40,064 --> 00:15:44,234
'Cause usually the little sister
is the younger sister.

248
00:15:44,318 --> 00:15:45,611
Which is me, right?

249
00:15:45,694 --> 00:15:49,865
Honey, I'm over 40, you're over 40.
None of us is young anymore.

250
00:15:49,949 --> 00:15:53,160
But I just turned over 40, all right?

251
00:15:53,243 --> 00:15:56,538
When I look back, I can see my 30s
right there. I can touch them.

252
00:15:56,622 --> 00:16:00,042
-Hold it!
-Clarice! Stop with that ball now!

253
00:16:00,125 --> 00:16:04,296
You don't see anything, Roberta.
Only diapers, pacifiers, school supplies.

254
00:16:04,380 --> 00:16:06,715
Where's the Roberta
who wanted a tribal tattoo?

255
00:16:06,799 --> 00:16:08,550
-Remember her?
-Geez.

256
00:16:08,634 --> 00:16:10,427
-Do you remember?
-No. Please.

257
00:16:10,511 --> 00:16:13,055
Thank God you didn't do it. Jesus Christ.

258
00:16:13,138 --> 00:16:16,141
Honestly, it's a shame I didn't do it.

259
00:16:16,225 --> 00:16:20,270
I should've done it, you know?
Like, a really bad tattoo.

260
00:16:20,354 --> 00:16:24,024
A flower on my groin.
To have a mark on my body.

261
00:16:24,108 --> 00:16:27,027
Telling a story
of a woman who just went for it.

262
00:16:27,111 --> 00:16:29,571
That lived life. Who did crazy things.

263
00:16:29,655 --> 00:16:31,991
-Love it.
-Oh my God!

264
00:16:32,074 --> 00:16:33,993
-What?
-There's no flour for the <i>farofa</i>.

265
00:16:34,076 --> 00:16:36,578
Shit, I almost died here, Roberta.

266
00:16:36,662 --> 00:16:40,290
Bianca, honey. Come eat a chicken heart.
Daddy saved it.

267
00:16:40,374 --> 00:16:41,917
Can I sleep at Fernanda's?

268
00:16:42,001 --> 00:16:43,877
-Tonight?
-Yeah.

269
00:16:43,961 --> 00:16:46,630
But, honey, it's Daddy's night.

270
00:16:46,714 --> 00:16:48,132
-Please.
-You have a game.

271
00:16:48,215 --> 00:16:50,050
No. You'll stay with Daddy.

272
00:16:50,134 --> 00:16:52,511
You have to eat so you can
crush it in the game tomorrow.

273
00:16:52,594 --> 00:16:55,014
-Yeah, Clacla, wait for Bianca.
-Honey?

274
00:16:55,597 --> 00:16:56,432
Got you!

275
00:16:56,515 --> 00:16:59,810
-Hey!
-Clarice, you're such a cheat, dude.

276
00:16:59,893 --> 00:17:01,437
-I'm not.
-Yes, you are.

277
00:17:01,520 --> 00:17:02,688
I'm not.

278
00:17:02,771 --> 00:17:04,606
Who has the ball, you or us?

279
00:17:16,160 --> 00:17:18,495
Thank God! Thank you, Lord!

280
00:17:18,579 --> 00:17:22,583
Everyone's gonna stuff their faces
with farofa today. That's it.

281
00:17:23,167 --> 00:17:24,710
Guaranteed constipation.

282
00:17:24,793 --> 00:17:27,171
Isn't it? Mommy found it…

283
00:17:28,047 --> 00:17:30,758
-What's that, Matheus?
-Stop!

284
00:17:30,841 --> 00:17:34,386
-Now. Let's go.
-I'm starting to feel it!

285
00:17:34,470 --> 00:17:36,513
-Let's go!
-Feeling it, Matheus.

286
00:17:36,597 --> 00:17:39,475
-Let's go!
-That's it!

287
00:17:41,351 --> 00:17:43,979
Use the space. Watch Mr. Cruise over here.

288
00:17:44,063 --> 00:17:46,815
-Give me the ball! Give it to me!
-No, I'm…

289
00:17:46,899 --> 00:17:48,859
-Give it to me!
-No!

290
00:17:49,860 --> 00:17:51,403
The meat is burning, man!

291
00:17:51,487 --> 00:17:54,281
Fred! Fred, watch the girls!

292
00:17:54,364 --> 00:17:56,742
They could explode, he wouldn't see it.

293
00:17:56,825 --> 00:17:59,328
I'm going to go to Salvador
to do some interviews for my thesis.

294
00:17:59,411 --> 00:18:02,873
-Really? Amazing!
-Yeah, and I'll spend a few days there.

295
00:18:02,956 --> 00:18:05,542
Salvador is everything! You should come.

296
00:18:05,626 --> 00:18:07,878
-Can you imagine?
-Can you imagine?

297
00:18:07,961 --> 00:18:09,755
I would love that.

298
00:18:11,173 --> 00:18:13,717
Oh, there's juice on Mommy's leg.

299
00:18:13,801 --> 00:18:17,137
How could I? Tell me, Renata.

300
00:18:17,221 --> 00:18:18,931
Tell me how I could do that.

301
00:18:19,014 --> 00:18:22,559
Tom Tom's adjusting to daycare this week.

302
00:18:22,643 --> 00:18:24,311
Oh my God, there's so much juice.

303
00:18:24,394 --> 00:18:25,938
-Give me the ball!
-No!

304
00:18:26,021 --> 00:18:27,481
Give me the ball.

305
00:18:27,564 --> 00:18:29,066
So much juice.

306
00:18:29,608 --> 00:18:31,735
But Tom Tom has a father, right?

307
00:18:31,819 --> 00:18:33,070
Work it!

308
00:18:33,153 --> 00:18:36,365
Or does the Constitution say
the mom's responsible for daycare?

309
00:18:41,286 --> 00:18:42,579
Clarice!

310
00:18:42,663 --> 00:18:45,582
-I told Clarice to stop with the ball.
-Ouch, Mom!

311
00:18:46,166 --> 00:18:47,167
Didn't I?

312
00:18:47,251 --> 00:18:48,961
-I did.
-Mom, ouch!

313
00:18:49,044 --> 00:18:51,505
No one listens. You know what I wanted?

314
00:18:51,588 --> 00:18:53,674
Let them. Right? Just let them.

315
00:18:53,757 --> 00:18:55,551
-Throw the ball. Go.
-Mom!

316
00:18:55,634 --> 00:18:59,138
Mom, Dad's asking
if you're going to set the table.

317
00:18:59,221 --> 00:19:00,597
What?

318
00:19:02,641 --> 00:19:04,309
Guys, wait a second.

319
00:19:04,393 --> 00:19:08,397
I heard Bianca is in the tennis
championship finals. Is that it?

320
00:19:08,480 --> 00:19:13,110
We are, right?
Because I'm always right there with her.

321
00:19:13,193 --> 00:19:15,988
If my daughter's dream is to be
a tennis player, it's my dream too.

322
00:19:16,071 --> 00:19:17,030
Right?

323
00:19:17,114 --> 00:19:17,948
Right.

324
00:19:26,832 --> 00:19:28,542
He wants to say something.

325
00:19:28,625 --> 00:19:33,297
Excuse me, I'd like to ask for a round
of applause to our barbecue chef!

326
00:19:33,380 --> 00:19:34,590
-Me?
-Yeah.

327
00:19:36,675 --> 00:19:39,136
Fred, I don't say so
as you're my best friend,

328
00:19:39,219 --> 00:19:43,640
but it was very nice of you
to make this barbecue for our families.

329
00:19:43,724 --> 00:19:48,228
-Thanks for letting me to be a part of it.
-Thanks for your words, my friend.

330
00:19:48,312 --> 00:19:49,980
I didn't do anything at all.

331
00:19:50,063 --> 00:19:54,693
I mean, obviously, everything I do
is for my wonderful family.

332
00:19:54,776 --> 00:19:56,445
A round of applause!

333
00:19:59,990 --> 00:20:03,493
And applause for the person
who bought the meat, made the salad,

334
00:20:03,577 --> 00:20:06,955
set the table, takes care of the children.
No applause?

335
00:20:07,039 --> 00:20:09,541
Of course.
A round of applause for Roberta.

336
00:20:10,459 --> 00:20:11,460
Of course.

337
00:20:13,879 --> 00:20:15,255
Are you that ungrateful?

338
00:20:15,339 --> 00:20:17,883
Let's give Mom a round of applause.
Come on!

339
00:20:18,967 --> 00:20:20,677
More emphasis.

340
00:20:21,720 --> 00:20:24,556
The older sister
won't applaud her little sister?

341
00:20:25,224 --> 00:20:26,350
Seriously.

342
00:20:26,433 --> 00:20:30,312
Wow, I always forget
that Aunt Renata is the oldest.

343
00:20:30,395 --> 00:20:33,649
-Doesn't seem like it.
-Is she? Really? That's bizarre.

344
00:20:34,149 --> 00:20:36,151
You want a chicken heart, honey?

345
00:20:36,235 --> 00:20:38,487
Take a chicken heart.
It's delicious, honey.

346
00:20:38,570 --> 00:20:40,280
<i>It's delicious, honey.</i>

347
00:20:51,250 --> 00:20:54,461
Honey, there are little capybaras
doing water aerobics.

348
00:20:54,544 --> 00:20:56,630
Geez, you have to see it.

349
00:21:00,050 --> 00:21:01,260
Yay!

350
00:21:02,219 --> 00:21:03,845
Go over there. To your side.

351
00:21:03,929 --> 00:21:07,015
Honey, my side's your side,
and your side's my side.

352
00:21:07,099 --> 00:21:08,350
Come on.

353
00:21:08,433 --> 00:21:10,602
-You smell good.
-That's great, huh?

354
00:21:11,436 --> 00:21:12,854
At least our scent doesn't age.

355
00:21:13,438 --> 00:21:17,609
A person can be 109 years old,
but their perfume will still smell great.

356
00:21:19,569 --> 00:21:22,114
-What are you talking about?
-I'm 42 years old.

357
00:21:22,197 --> 00:21:24,950
But I look worn out. I look 109 years old.

358
00:21:25,033 --> 00:21:27,786
But then again,
I take care of five children.

359
00:21:27,869 --> 00:21:29,538
-How would I look?
-You're beautiful.

360
00:21:29,621 --> 00:21:31,456
Wait, "five"? We have four children.

361
00:21:31,540 --> 00:21:33,834
You're the fifth.
You can't do anything yourself.

362
00:21:33,917 --> 00:21:35,585
-Me? Give me an example.
-Mm-hmm.

363
00:21:36,628 --> 00:21:39,214
Honey, where's my towel?

364
00:21:40,549 --> 00:21:42,217
Honey, didn't you buy butter?

365
00:21:43,802 --> 00:21:45,929
Roberta, have you seen my salmon shirt?

366
00:21:46,013 --> 00:21:47,723
It's like I have five children.

367
00:21:47,806 --> 00:21:51,310
You think asking for help's bad?
It's a sign of humility.

368
00:21:51,393 --> 00:21:52,936
To say, "I can't do this alone."

369
00:21:53,020 --> 00:21:56,815
Honey, you have experience in the house.
You know the rhythm. I won't mess with it.

370
00:21:56,898 --> 00:22:00,152
-You're joking?
-Betinha, you're overreacting, honey.

371
00:22:00,235 --> 00:22:04,865
-Your life's just like any other mom's.
-Other moms are exhausted, overwhelmed.

372
00:22:04,948 --> 00:22:06,950
Especially without a supportive husband.

373
00:22:07,034 --> 00:22:09,369
I can't believe
you're saying I don't help.

374
00:22:09,453 --> 00:22:11,830
Don't I feed Tom Tom when you ask me to?

375
00:22:11,913 --> 00:22:13,749
Really, it's not about helping.

376
00:22:13,832 --> 00:22:15,417
It's sharing the workload.

377
00:22:15,500 --> 00:22:18,920
Doing what needs to be done
without me having to ask!

378
00:22:19,004 --> 00:22:22,257
I won't argue. Know why?
You don't know what I go through.

379
00:22:22,341 --> 00:22:24,634
You don't know what I go through at work.

380
00:22:24,718 --> 00:22:28,096
Honestly, I think it's a privilege
you get the opportunity

381
00:22:28,180 --> 00:22:30,932
to spend your days at home

382
00:22:31,016 --> 00:22:33,310
with the most important thing
in life, our kids.

383
00:22:33,393 --> 00:22:35,604
So, I said what I wanted.

384
00:22:35,687 --> 00:22:37,564
That's it. I'd love to be in your shoes.

385
00:22:37,647 --> 00:22:38,857
-Oh, really?
-Really.

386
00:22:38,940 --> 00:22:41,109
Swear on your children's health?

387
00:22:42,986 --> 00:22:45,322
Think carefully before you answer.

388
00:22:47,115 --> 00:22:48,033
I swear.

389
00:22:48,116 --> 00:22:51,453
Roberta, I can't believe
you're doing something so crazy.

390
00:22:51,536 --> 00:22:53,830
Didn't you want to be in my shoes?

391
00:22:53,914 --> 00:22:55,999
-This is your chance.
-It's bad timing.

392
00:22:56,083 --> 00:22:57,667
I'm trying for a promotion.

393
00:22:57,751 --> 00:22:59,795
-Dante won't get off my back.
-Ten days, Fred.

394
00:22:59,878 --> 00:23:02,339
Really.
You wanted to be in my shoes so bad,

395
00:23:02,422 --> 00:23:05,884
enjoying your family
and those beautiful children of yours.

396
00:23:05,967 --> 00:23:09,846
-So here's your chance.
-You're only thinking about yourself.

397
00:23:09,930 --> 00:23:12,516
Not about your children,
who are so nervous about this.

398
00:23:12,599 --> 00:23:14,935
Tom Tom can't process mom's absence.

399
00:23:15,018 --> 00:23:18,397
Guys, like I said,
Mommy's going on a trip.

400
00:23:18,480 --> 00:23:20,774
Good for you, Mom. I wish I could go.

401
00:23:20,857 --> 00:23:22,818
Yeah, Mom, go. Go have fun.

402
00:23:23,485 --> 00:23:25,570
-Thank you, sweethearts.
-Mommy.

403
00:23:33,370 --> 00:23:34,579
Dad!

404
00:23:34,663 --> 00:23:38,166
She'll listen to you. She will.
Go on, honey.

405
00:23:39,459 --> 00:23:42,462
Tell Mommy what you were
so nervously telling Daddy.

406
00:23:42,546 --> 00:23:45,257
-What, honey?
-We're nervous about staying with Dad.

407
00:23:45,340 --> 00:23:46,341
No!

408
00:23:46,842 --> 00:23:50,262
Not about staying with Dad.
Staying with Dad's wonderful.

409
00:23:50,345 --> 00:23:53,056
They're really nervous
to be without Mommy.

410
00:23:53,140 --> 00:23:54,683
-Isn't that right?
-I messed up.

411
00:23:54,766 --> 00:23:58,019
-You're afraid of the unknown?
-What "unknown," honey?

412
00:23:58,103 --> 00:24:01,815
-It's my children, my house…
-Great. So come with me real quick.

413
00:24:03,650 --> 00:24:04,693
It's all here.

414
00:24:04,776 --> 00:24:08,822
Tuesdays, Thursdays, Clarice's jazz dance.
Malu has urban dance on Wednesdays.

415
00:24:08,905 --> 00:24:11,741
João and Malu have swimming classes
on Mondays and Wednesdays.

416
00:24:11,825 --> 00:24:14,494
Clacla has swimming classes
on Wednesdays and Fridays.

417
00:24:14,578 --> 00:24:16,204
-Cool.
-And I'm adding you

418
00:24:16,288 --> 00:24:20,333
to Clarice's swimming group,
João's swimming group,

419
00:24:20,417 --> 00:24:22,961
and Malu's swimming group right now.

420
00:24:23,044 --> 00:24:27,174
Don't worry. Jazz and urban dance
have only one group for the whole studio.

421
00:24:27,257 --> 00:24:28,592
I'll add you to it too.

422
00:24:29,176 --> 00:24:32,554
Oh, and I'll add you to the school group.

423
00:24:32,637 --> 00:24:35,765
There's just one group
for all the parents.

424
00:24:35,849 --> 00:24:38,101
-You'll love it. I'm adding you.
-Great.

425
00:24:38,185 --> 00:24:41,062
Don't post stuff
on politics, soccer, or jokes.

426
00:24:41,146 --> 00:24:43,482
They have enough to talk about all day.

427
00:24:43,565 --> 00:24:44,816
No need to innovate.

428
00:24:49,738 --> 00:24:51,364
What is this? Roberta?

429
00:24:51,448 --> 00:24:52,324
NEW CHLORINE BRAND?

430
00:24:52,407 --> 00:24:53,700
THAT GIRL WHO BITES OTHER KIDS

431
00:24:53,783 --> 00:24:55,368
FERNANDA GOT OUT OF JAZZ 10 MINUTES EARLY

432
00:24:55,452 --> 00:24:56,328
Roberta?

433
00:24:56,411 --> 00:24:58,705
Guys, ten days will fly by.

434
00:24:58,788 --> 00:25:00,916
And Salvador is so close.

435
00:25:01,541 --> 00:25:04,419
Everything will be fine.
Listen to your dad.

436
00:25:04,503 --> 00:25:05,754
-I love you.
-Honey…

437
00:25:07,797 --> 00:25:10,300
Mommy loves you. Bye. Be good, okay?

438
00:25:10,383 --> 00:25:14,137
-Have fun, Mom.
-Don't forget to bring us presents.

439
00:25:14,221 --> 00:25:15,180
Go nuts, Mom.

440
00:25:15,263 --> 00:25:17,015
Don't go nuts, okay, honey?

441
00:25:17,098 --> 00:25:19,059
Come back in one piece, God.

442
00:25:19,893 --> 00:25:21,520
Bye.

443
00:25:22,062 --> 00:25:25,357
-Bye.
-Bye. Mommy loves you.

444
00:25:26,608 --> 00:25:27,817
Mommy…

445
00:25:28,944 --> 00:25:31,071
-Let's play. I'll start.
-I'm in.

446
00:25:31,154 --> 00:25:32,364
Dear Lord.

447
00:25:39,621 --> 00:25:40,830
Just a second.

448
00:25:42,374 --> 00:25:43,750
For the love of God, man.

449
00:25:43,833 --> 00:25:46,628
I abandoned my children, Renata.

450
00:25:46,711 --> 00:25:49,965
-Oh my God, ten days. I'm a monster.
-No, you're not.

451
00:25:50,048 --> 00:25:52,592
I only think of myself. I'm so tired.

452
00:25:52,676 --> 00:25:55,887
I only think about how tired I am,
and that's selfish.

453
00:25:55,971 --> 00:25:57,681
They're kids. Go back, sir.

454
00:25:57,764 --> 00:25:59,182
-Don't go back.
-I won't.

455
00:25:59,266 --> 00:26:01,184
-My chest hurts.
-Calm down.

456
00:26:01,268 --> 00:26:03,228
-I don't wanna go.
-It's fine.

457
00:26:03,311 --> 00:26:06,398
It's only ten days, relax.
They're happy for you.

458
00:26:06,481 --> 00:26:08,275
Did you hear this baby crying?

459
00:26:08,358 --> 00:26:09,568
Is it Tom Tom?

460
00:26:09,651 --> 00:26:10,777
-It's Tom Tom.
-Roberta…

461
00:26:10,860 --> 00:26:12,904
He must be thinking,
"Why'd Mommy leave me?"

462
00:26:12,988 --> 00:26:17,492
We're in the car, going to the airport.
There's no baby here. Right, sir?

463
00:26:17,576 --> 00:26:19,119
-No baby.
-It's a sign.

464
00:26:19,202 --> 00:26:21,371
It's Tom Tom.
Mothers have superhuman hearing.

465
00:26:21,454 --> 00:26:23,290
You wouldn't know, you haven't lived it.

466
00:26:23,373 --> 00:26:25,375
-It's not Tom Tom.
-I have a little one.

467
00:26:25,458 --> 00:26:29,504
It's not Tom Tom. And even if it is,
he has a father and three siblings.

468
00:26:29,588 --> 00:26:32,299
-He even has Simone.
-He has Simone.

469
00:26:32,382 --> 00:26:35,093
-No one's going to die.
-He has Simone. Thanks.

470
00:26:35,176 --> 00:26:37,596
-No one will die.
-We'll have fun, right?

471
00:26:37,679 --> 00:26:40,473
-It'll be great!
-It will be good, right?

472
00:26:40,557 --> 00:26:43,685
-Yes, it'll be good, great.
-We'll have a piña colada!

473
00:26:43,768 --> 00:26:45,312
What have I done?!

474
00:26:46,855 --> 00:26:49,441
<i>How could I ever live</i>

475
00:26:49,524 --> 00:26:54,487
<i>Without your, without your</i>
<i>Without your company?</i>

476
00:26:54,571 --> 00:26:57,532
Son, I've sung this 86 times.
How about in English?

477
00:27:00,493 --> 00:27:03,121
Nobody can stand two hours
47 minutes to put a kid to bed,

478
00:27:03,204 --> 00:27:05,707
adding two plus seven is nine…
that's a lot of time.

479
00:27:14,966 --> 00:27:17,302
Honey, it's late.
Turn that off and let's go to bed.

480
00:27:17,385 --> 00:27:20,305
{\an8}Dad, are you sure we'll survive
without Mom?

481
00:27:20,388 --> 00:27:21,264
Yes.

482
00:27:23,600 --> 00:27:24,601
Let's go to bed.

483
00:27:37,947 --> 00:27:40,575
My sweethearts.
Beautiful kids, good morning.

484
00:27:40,659 --> 00:27:42,827
-It's not!
-We missed first period.

485
00:27:42,911 --> 00:27:44,621
How irresponsible of you!

486
00:27:44,704 --> 00:27:47,040
-Why didn't you get up?
-No one turned the AC off.

487
00:27:48,208 --> 00:27:50,418
Let's go, guys. Let's go.

488
00:28:08,603 --> 00:28:09,938
Everything's under control.

489
00:28:10,021 --> 00:28:13,316
You'll have a delicious breakfast
made by Daddy, who loves you very much.

490
00:28:13,400 --> 00:28:16,152
We're about to miss second period.

491
00:28:16,236 --> 00:28:18,113
Hey, leave it. Shut up.

492
00:28:18,196 --> 00:28:21,908
Sweethearts, if you thought
you'd miss Mommy's delicious food,

493
00:28:21,991 --> 00:28:23,618
look what you're getting.

494
00:28:23,702 --> 00:28:26,246
-No. What is this?
-Daddy's delicious food.

495
00:28:26,329 --> 00:28:27,872
Look at all these options.

496
00:28:28,540 --> 00:28:31,584
This is good, guys.
So delicious! How is it, honey?

497
00:28:33,503 --> 00:28:35,296
What kind of cheese is this?

498
00:28:35,380 --> 00:28:39,008
-No. Too much fried food.
-You always ask to go to the US.

499
00:28:39,092 --> 00:28:39,926
Fried food?

500
00:28:40,009 --> 00:28:43,388
That's all they eat in the US, honey.
You can't complain.

501
00:28:43,471 --> 00:28:46,266
It's hard to do things in a rush,
but this is delicious.

502
00:28:46,349 --> 00:28:49,853
Everyone needs to eat well
to get to school strong, healthy,

503
00:28:49,936 --> 00:28:51,896
to learn a lot of wonderful things.

504
00:28:51,980 --> 00:28:55,024
-Eat some grapes.
-Dad, put some butter on my bread.

505
00:28:55,108 --> 00:28:58,069
Don't you have a mom, honey?
I mean, don't you have hands?

506
00:28:58,153 --> 00:29:01,114
This has nothing to do with mothers.
I meant hands!

507
00:29:01,197 --> 00:29:03,366
Spread the butter
with your own hands, okay?

508
00:29:03,450 --> 00:29:06,661
Wow, Dad, this breakfast is delicious.

509
00:29:06,745 --> 00:29:09,247
You really surprised me.

510
00:29:09,330 --> 00:29:11,750
The thing is, there's only enough for me.

511
00:29:11,833 --> 00:29:13,626
-We need more.
-Next time, you help me.

512
00:29:13,710 --> 00:29:15,336
-Come on.
-You can have mine.

513
00:29:15,420 --> 00:29:17,046
I don't want this, it's disgusting.

514
00:29:17,130 --> 00:29:19,924
Malu, I won't let you say
the food's disgusting.

515
00:29:20,008 --> 00:29:24,679
You do all kinds of disgusting things.
Who wants delicious eggs made by Daddy?

516
00:29:24,763 --> 00:29:27,849
-Damn it, Clarice, come on!
-No, wait. Malu, no.

517
00:29:27,932 --> 00:29:30,310
-Stop!
-Girls, stop it right now.

518
00:29:30,393 --> 00:29:31,603
-Don't burp.
-Ew!

519
00:29:31,686 --> 00:29:33,897
-Good one, João! Burp!
-Do not burp.

520
00:29:33,980 --> 00:29:37,484
-Burp!
-Burp!

521
00:29:37,567 --> 00:29:40,695
Do not-- Do not burp!

522
00:29:41,321 --> 00:29:43,281
Are you trying to drive me crazy?

523
00:29:43,364 --> 00:29:48,077
It's only breakfast. Everyone's going
to school on an empty stomach!

524
00:29:48,161 --> 00:29:50,830
With your clothes all dirty!
I don't even care.

525
00:29:50,914 --> 00:29:52,540
Don't like what I said and did?

526
00:29:52,624 --> 00:29:56,878
I don't care, because I've had enough!
I've had enough!

527
00:29:56,961 --> 00:29:58,838
-Mr. Fred?
-Simone!

528
00:29:58,922 --> 00:30:00,089
Is everything okay?

529
00:30:00,173 --> 00:30:02,634
Everything's great.

530
00:30:03,551 --> 00:30:06,805
My credibility as a father
has taken a bit of a hit.

531
00:30:06,888 --> 00:30:10,517
But you didn't see the moments
that led up to this.

532
00:30:10,600 --> 00:30:12,560
It's only the first day.

533
00:30:13,144 --> 00:30:15,230
-Let's go, Dad!
-Let's go, Dad, we're late.

534
00:30:15,313 --> 00:30:16,564
Okay! Calm down.

535
00:30:16,648 --> 00:30:19,192
This kid won't stop pooping!

536
00:30:19,275 --> 00:30:22,153
I don't understand anything he says.
Simone, how are you?

537
00:30:22,237 --> 00:30:26,491
I know you work three times a week,
but could you come for ten straight days?

538
00:30:26,574 --> 00:30:28,243
It's for the kids, mostly.

539
00:30:31,871 --> 00:30:33,790
-All right, Mr. Fred.
-Thank you so much.

540
00:30:33,873 --> 00:30:34,749
-Let's go.
-Yes.

541
00:30:34,833 --> 00:30:36,376
-Yes!
-Come here, son.

542
00:30:36,459 --> 00:30:38,545
-Here's Tom Tom's mango.
-Mango!

543
00:30:38,628 --> 00:30:39,629
Thank you.

544
00:30:40,255 --> 00:30:42,549
-I don't understand you.
-Bye, my dear.

545
00:30:47,470 --> 00:30:49,681
-I missed two classes.
-You didn't miss anything.

546
00:30:49,764 --> 00:30:52,225
You got to spend time
with your family, your siblings.

547
00:30:52,308 --> 00:30:54,894
Eating mango, everyone's happy.
What was the class?

548
00:30:54,978 --> 00:30:57,063
-Geography.
-Geography?

549
00:30:57,146 --> 00:30:59,774
Geography is mango, it's land, it's <i>miome</i>.

550
00:30:59,858 --> 00:31:00,859
Biome!

551
00:31:00,942 --> 00:31:02,610
See? I don't even remember.

552
00:31:02,694 --> 00:31:05,071
If you're not gonna be a geographer,
you don't need…

553
00:31:05,154 --> 00:31:08,741
Thanks. You don't need Geography.
Son, wet wipes, please.

554
00:31:08,825 --> 00:31:11,202
I had two Portuguese classes,
which I missed.

555
00:31:11,286 --> 00:31:12,996
We're speaking Portuguese now.

556
00:31:13,079 --> 00:31:14,956
You didn't miss it. Do you understand me?

557
00:31:15,039 --> 00:31:17,125
We're communicating
perfectly in Portuguese,

558
00:31:17,208 --> 00:31:18,418
so you know Portuguese.

559
00:31:18,501 --> 00:31:19,961
Wet wipes. He's all dirty.

560
00:31:20,044 --> 00:31:21,796
-What class did Clacla have?
-English.

561
00:31:21,880 --> 00:31:24,632
English? But-- Wet wipes.
No one learns English in school.

562
00:31:24,716 --> 00:31:27,010
You didn't enroll us in an English course

563
00:31:27,093 --> 00:31:29,596
because you said
we were already learning at school.

564
00:31:29,679 --> 00:31:31,180
-Did I say that?
-Yes.

565
00:31:31,264 --> 00:31:34,225
No, that's for later.
We'll learn English at another time.

566
00:31:34,309 --> 00:31:36,019
I don't understand you, okay?

567
00:31:36,102 --> 00:31:37,896
I don't understand you, honey.

568
00:31:37,979 --> 00:31:40,732
-Wet wipes, João!
-I'm looking, Dad, they're not here!

569
00:31:40,815 --> 00:31:42,775
-How?
-You didn't put them here.

570
00:31:42,859 --> 00:31:45,236
-If you had, they would be here.
-No wipes. Let's go?

571
00:31:45,320 --> 00:31:47,655
-Let's go!
-Let's go. Finally.

572
00:31:47,739 --> 00:31:48,865
Help me with him.

573
00:32:03,129 --> 00:32:04,172
Oh, sweethearts.

574
00:32:04,839 --> 00:32:07,467
-Have a nice day.
-Dad, why did you stop here?

575
00:32:07,550 --> 00:32:09,510
What do you mean? It's your school.

576
00:32:10,094 --> 00:32:12,889
We don't go here anymore,
we switched schools last year.

577
00:32:21,105 --> 00:32:24,108
<i>The frog won't wash his feet</i>

578
00:32:24,192 --> 00:32:27,111
<i>He won't wash them</i>
<i>Because he doesn't want to</i>

579
00:32:27,195 --> 00:32:30,323
<i>He lives down by the little pond</i>

580
00:32:30,406 --> 00:32:33,242
<i>He won't wash his feet</i>
<i>Because he doesn't want to</i>

581
00:32:33,326 --> 00:32:36,454
<i>What a stinky smell!</i>

582
00:32:36,537 --> 00:32:40,375
<i>Little butterfly's in the kitchen</i>

583
00:32:40,458 --> 00:32:44,629
<i>Making chocolates for her godmother</i>

584
00:32:44,712 --> 00:32:48,383
<i>Poti, poti</i>
<i>Wooden leg</i>

585
00:32:48,466 --> 00:32:52,679
<i>Glass eye</i>
<i>And a woodpecker's beak, beak, beak…</i>

586
00:32:52,762 --> 00:32:54,222
Now, really fast.

587
00:32:54,305 --> 00:32:55,515
Just a second.

588
00:32:56,182 --> 00:32:58,184
It's the same song, but faster.

589
00:32:58,267 --> 00:33:00,853
<i>Making chocolates for her godmother</i>

590
00:33:00,937 --> 00:33:03,564
<i>Poti, poti</i>
<i>Wooden leg…</i>

591
00:33:03,648 --> 00:33:04,899
It's the same song.

592
00:33:05,441 --> 00:33:08,111
<i>My love told me…</i>

593
00:33:08,194 --> 00:33:09,362
Son, say goodbye to Dad.

594
00:33:09,445 --> 00:33:13,825
<i>That the flower of the field is rosemary…</i>

595
00:33:13,908 --> 00:33:17,078
-Very good!
-He's settled in.

596
00:33:17,578 --> 00:33:18,955
He's great, right, son?

597
00:33:21,833 --> 00:33:23,418
Can you stay a little longer?

598
00:33:25,169 --> 00:33:28,715
<i>Rosemary, golden rosemary</i>

599
00:33:28,798 --> 00:33:32,719
<i>That grew in the field</i>
<i>Without ever being sown</i>

600
00:33:32,802 --> 00:33:35,346
It was completely unexpected, guys.

601
00:33:35,430 --> 00:33:37,849
And since I had
a few vacation days I needed to take,

602
00:33:37,932 --> 00:33:40,309
it all worked out,
because she really had to go.

603
00:33:40,393 --> 00:33:43,187
And it's only ten days, right?
Ten days fly by.

604
00:33:43,271 --> 00:33:45,481
But it's the opening week
for the new branch.

605
00:33:45,565 --> 00:33:46,816
-True.
-Not a good time.

606
00:33:46,899 --> 00:33:50,486
It's family, guys.
We do anything for family.

607
00:33:50,570 --> 00:33:52,196
Speaking of family, Pontes,

608
00:33:52,280 --> 00:33:54,699
how is that wonderful wife of yours, uh…

609
00:33:54,782 --> 00:33:56,701
-Ivone.
-Ivone, wonderful Ivone.

610
00:33:57,368 --> 00:33:59,412
I asked Roberta to bring back some gifts.

611
00:33:59,495 --> 00:34:00,955
No, there's no need.

612
00:34:01,039 --> 00:34:02,999
Stop it, Pontes, don't be like that.

613
00:34:03,082 --> 00:34:05,668
Who doesn't love
those little <i>cocadas </i>from Bahia?

614
00:34:05,752 --> 00:34:07,879
I asked her to bring 10, 15, 20 of them.

615
00:34:07,962 --> 00:34:09,630
-Who doesn't love them?
-A diabetic?

616
00:34:10,798 --> 00:34:14,260
I really wanted to thank you
for the doctor you recommended.

617
00:34:14,343 --> 00:34:15,887
My wife is very happy with him.

618
00:34:15,970 --> 00:34:18,014
No worries, Mr. Pontes, I'm happy to help.

619
00:34:18,681 --> 00:34:21,517
Speaking of gifts,
my wife is going to New York.

620
00:34:21,601 --> 00:34:26,272
She can bring back some perfume,
a purse, a real gift.

621
00:34:26,355 --> 00:34:28,024
-No, there's no need.
-Yes.

622
00:34:28,566 --> 00:34:31,444
And don't worry,
this trip was already planned,

623
00:34:31,527 --> 00:34:32,695
I won't miss any work.

624
00:34:33,654 --> 00:34:35,615
There's no need. Nonsense.

625
00:34:41,245 --> 00:34:42,497
SWIMMING CLASS 1
SWIMMING CLASS 2

626
00:34:42,580 --> 00:34:44,123
What's the need to connect human beings?

627
00:34:44,207 --> 00:34:46,000
STUDENTS' PARENTS GROUP
DANCE CLASSES - PARENTS

628
00:34:46,084 --> 00:34:47,794
Humans hate each other.
I'll mute everything.

629
00:34:55,551 --> 00:34:56,969
Quiet, turn it off.

630
00:35:19,242 --> 00:35:21,744
God, my thigh.
You should've done it, okay?

631
00:35:21,828 --> 00:35:23,579
-No way.
-You'll regret it.

632
00:35:23,663 --> 00:35:25,248
Everyone's looking.

633
00:35:25,331 --> 00:35:27,875
Yeah, because you're such a tourist.

634
00:35:27,959 --> 00:35:30,419
-No, it's pretty. Everyone loves it.
-I just met her.

635
00:35:30,962 --> 00:35:33,923
-Everyone's looking.
-You're not like me. I'm a local.

636
00:35:34,006 --> 00:35:35,508
People think I'm a local.

637
00:35:35,591 --> 00:35:38,678
-Wow, she's a-- Sure, she's a local.
-What are you doing?

638
00:35:38,761 --> 00:35:39,595
Calling Fred?

639
00:35:39,679 --> 00:35:40,680
No.

640
00:35:41,472 --> 00:35:42,473
Calling my informant.

641
00:35:46,769 --> 00:35:47,770
<i>Hi, Ms. Roberta.</i>

642
00:35:47,854 --> 00:35:51,107
Simone! Simone, my love, I miss you.

643
00:35:51,190 --> 00:35:52,692
How was the first day? Tell me.

644
00:35:52,775 --> 00:35:53,860
Terrible.

645
00:35:53,943 --> 00:35:55,069
Great!

646
00:35:55,153 --> 00:35:56,571
What happened? I want details.

647
00:35:56,654 --> 00:35:58,030
Who did what? What happened?

648
00:35:58,114 --> 00:36:00,241
Mr. Fred ran me over.

649
00:36:00,324 --> 00:36:02,535
I know, honey. He does that.

650
00:36:02,618 --> 00:36:04,453
He doesn't give us a chance.

651
00:36:04,537 --> 00:36:08,207
-He just gets in our way. I know that.
-No, Ms. Roberta.

652
00:36:08,291 --> 00:36:09,584
You don't understand.

653
00:36:09,667 --> 00:36:11,460
He ran me over with his car.

654
00:36:12,086 --> 00:36:13,171
He hit me with his car.

655
00:36:13,254 --> 00:36:14,797
-My God.
-<i>I went to the hospital.</i>

656
00:36:14,881 --> 00:36:17,383
Simone, are you okay?

657
00:36:17,466 --> 00:36:19,552
Well, I'm here, resting.

658
00:36:19,635 --> 00:36:22,221
I won't be able to go on for a week.
I just can't.

659
00:36:22,305 --> 00:36:24,765
-Of course.
<i>-But look, if you want,</i>

660
00:36:24,849 --> 00:36:28,102
I can send my niece to help Mr. Fred.

661
00:36:28,186 --> 00:36:32,607
And if I were you, I would want that,
because things are not good over there.

662
00:36:32,690 --> 00:36:36,110
Really? Things are not good.

663
00:36:36,194 --> 00:36:38,112
My niece is excellent.

664
00:36:38,196 --> 00:36:40,406
"Excellent" is a bit much, Simone.

665
00:36:40,489 --> 00:36:42,408
Yeah. That's not what I'm looking for.

666
00:36:42,491 --> 00:36:45,578
She'd do everything
while Fred sits back and relaxes?

667
00:36:45,661 --> 00:36:46,495
No, thank you.

668
00:36:46,579 --> 00:36:49,874
To be honest,
there's nothing excellent about her.

669
00:36:49,957 --> 00:36:53,711
<i>She's never worked in a family home,</i>
<i>can't keep a job,</i>

670
00:36:53,794 --> 00:36:57,423
<i>she came here to try her luck</i>
<i>and now here she is, living off me.</i>

671
00:36:57,506 --> 00:36:59,258
That's what I call excellent.

672
00:36:59,342 --> 00:37:01,135
Love it. Great résumé.

673
00:37:01,219 --> 00:37:03,137
Go ahead and send her to my house.

674
00:37:03,221 --> 00:37:05,890
<i>I'm really glad I found a job for her.</i>

675
00:37:05,973 --> 00:37:09,644
<i>And she can give Mr. Fred</i>
<i>a little help, right?</i>

676
00:37:09,727 --> 00:37:13,773
A little. I mean a little.
I don't want her doing everything for him.

677
00:37:13,856 --> 00:37:15,441
Don't worry. It's a deal.

678
00:37:16,025 --> 00:37:17,944
-Bye, get well soon.
-<i>Okay, bye.</i>

679
00:37:18,027 --> 00:37:19,111
Look…

680
00:37:19,195 --> 00:37:20,446
She's gone.

681
00:37:21,113 --> 00:37:23,366
-Fred ran over Simone.
-Huh?

682
00:37:23,449 --> 00:37:24,450
Come on!

683
00:37:29,455 --> 00:37:30,581
Good job, honey.

684
00:37:34,752 --> 00:37:37,380
-What do you want?
-I don't get what he's saying.

685
00:37:37,880 --> 00:37:39,340
Red, right? Red.

686
00:37:40,174 --> 00:37:41,968
Guys, please, give me a break.

687
00:37:42,051 --> 00:37:43,970
Please, take a breath, stop running.

688
00:37:44,053 --> 00:37:44,971
Guys, please.

689
00:37:45,054 --> 00:37:47,306
You keep leaving
your clothes all over the house.

690
00:37:47,390 --> 00:37:48,474
-Dad.
-Yes, honey.

691
00:37:48,557 --> 00:37:50,017
Where's my birth certificate?

692
00:37:50,101 --> 00:37:51,602
Oh my God. Is that a challenge?

693
00:37:51,686 --> 00:37:53,813
How am I supposed to know that?

694
00:37:53,896 --> 00:37:56,482
Well, you're my father.
Why don't you know?

695
00:37:56,565 --> 00:37:59,694
Dads need to know everything?
Why do you need it?

696
00:37:59,777 --> 00:38:02,405
I want to know what time I was born
to make my birth chart.

697
00:38:04,115 --> 00:38:06,284
-You were born at 9 p.m.
-You're making that up.

698
00:38:06,367 --> 00:38:09,245
-No one is born on the dot like that.
-You were, honey.

699
00:38:09,328 --> 00:38:11,414
The doctor was great.
Had a big beard. He said,

700
00:38:11,497 --> 00:38:14,208
"Congratulations,
your daughter is extremely punctual."

701
00:38:14,292 --> 00:38:15,876
And you still are. That's it.

702
00:38:15,960 --> 00:38:18,421
I can't believe it, Dad.
You're making fun of me.

703
00:38:18,504 --> 00:38:19,547
Absolutely.

704
00:38:19,630 --> 00:38:22,883
And please stop leaving all this stuff
around the house.

705
00:38:22,967 --> 00:38:25,553
-That's not mine.
-It's not? Huh.

706
00:38:25,636 --> 00:38:26,554
Malu…

707
00:38:30,474 --> 00:38:31,309
Weird.

708
00:38:35,354 --> 00:38:37,857
João. Look at all these clothes.

709
00:38:37,940 --> 00:38:39,775
-Give me that.
-Huh?

710
00:38:42,320 --> 00:38:45,489
What is this?

711
00:38:45,573 --> 00:38:48,200
-I was studying with a friend.
-What friend?

712
00:38:50,328 --> 00:38:52,872
Clacla! What are you holding,
for God's sake?

713
00:38:52,955 --> 00:38:54,957
What is this? What is this, kids?

714
00:38:55,041 --> 00:38:56,709
Go away, cockroach!

