00:51:22,662 --> 00:51:24,831
Dad, do something.

956
00:51:24,915 --> 00:51:26,416
-What now?
-Oh, no.

957
00:51:27,834 --> 00:51:31,671
Guys, I need to get to Tom Tom
before he reaches that outlet, okay?

958
00:51:31,755 --> 00:51:33,215
-It's fine.
-What are you doing?

959
00:51:33,298 --> 00:51:34,716
-What do you mean?
-Trust me.

960
00:51:34,800 --> 00:51:36,802
-Everything will be fine.
-No, Dad!

961
00:51:36,885 --> 00:51:39,471
Guys, everything will be fine.
It's Daddy, okay?

962
00:51:39,554 --> 00:51:42,057
-Oh my God.
-This is not going to work.

963
00:51:42,140 --> 00:51:43,600
-It's fine.
-Be careful, Dad.

964
00:51:43,683 --> 00:51:44,893
Everything will be fine.

965
00:51:45,435 --> 00:51:46,603
-Dad!
-Dad!

966
00:51:47,187 --> 00:51:49,606
-Dad, hold on tighter.
-Just a second.

967
00:51:50,482 --> 00:51:52,526
-Dad, hold on.
-Just a second.

968
00:51:53,068 --> 00:51:54,069
Jesus…

969
00:51:55,278 --> 00:51:57,072
Put your foot down first.

970
00:51:57,155 --> 00:51:59,282
-There.
-Daddy's here.

971
00:51:59,866 --> 00:52:01,118
It's gonna work, guys.

972
00:52:03,578 --> 00:52:06,456
It's going to work, okay?
I got this far already.

973
00:52:06,540 --> 00:52:08,792
I got this far, this is already…

974
00:52:08,875 --> 00:52:09,793
It's already…

975
00:52:10,418 --> 00:52:13,171
-Guys, is that Mr. Fred?
-Yes.

976
00:52:13,255 --> 00:52:15,632
-Yes. We don't have the key.
-I have the key.

977
00:52:15,715 --> 00:52:17,300
Mr. Fred! The key!

978
00:52:17,384 --> 00:52:18,885
I have the key, Mr. Fred!

979
00:52:18,969 --> 00:52:20,011
-Where?
-Here!

980
00:52:21,680 --> 00:52:23,098
My God!

981
00:52:23,181 --> 00:52:24,724
-He's screwed.
-What do we do?

982
00:52:24,808 --> 00:52:26,226
He passed out.

983
00:52:34,943 --> 00:52:35,944
You scared me, dude.

984
00:52:36,027 --> 00:52:39,030
-Where are my kids, Matheus?
-Relax, they're at home.

985
00:52:39,114 --> 00:52:41,741
They're with the new girl
that's replacing Simone.

986
00:52:42,617 --> 00:52:43,994
She's such a character.

987
00:52:44,703 --> 00:52:47,372
But everything's okay, relax. Calm down.

988
00:53:20,906 --> 00:53:23,992
Here. Look, guys, it's like that.

989
00:53:24,075 --> 00:53:25,827
Oh, that's so pretty.

990
00:53:25,911 --> 00:53:27,704
The "Clean me up, Mommy" position.

991
00:53:27,787 --> 00:53:30,040
Put your legs up just like Tom Tom.

992
00:53:30,123 --> 00:53:31,416
Got it?

993
00:53:31,499 --> 00:53:33,293
That's the figure-eight move, guys.

994
00:53:33,376 --> 00:53:37,756
But I want you to do the figure-four move,
the one we practiced earlier.

995
00:53:37,839 --> 00:53:38,715
-Okay?
-Okay.

996
00:53:38,798 --> 00:53:41,676
Front, side, back, side.

997
00:53:42,260 --> 00:53:44,596
Is it hard? Yes.
Because that's a funk classic.

998
00:53:44,679 --> 00:53:46,306
Even your dad knows this one.

999
00:53:46,389 --> 00:53:50,101
Now, faster. Front, side, back, side.

1000
00:53:50,185 --> 00:53:52,103
You're laughing, huh?
You think it's funny?

1001
00:53:52,187 --> 00:53:53,396
I'll teach you something.

1002
00:53:53,897 --> 00:53:55,941
I'll teach you how to approach a girl

1003
00:53:56,024 --> 00:54:00,487
to make her weak in the knees,
but not to qualify as harassment.

1004
00:54:00,570 --> 00:54:01,655
-Got it?
-Got it. Go on.

1005
00:54:01,738 --> 00:54:04,407
Calm down, in my own time, man.
Relax, big guy.

1006
00:54:04,491 --> 00:54:05,450
Let's go.

1007
00:54:11,373 --> 00:54:12,707
Hey. How are you doing?

1008
00:54:13,375 --> 00:54:15,752
That's it. You say that, and that's it.

1009
00:54:15,835 --> 00:54:17,712
That's it. Can he touch her?

1010
00:54:17,796 --> 00:54:19,673
-No.
-No. If you touch her, you're out.

1011
00:54:19,756 --> 00:54:20,632
You're out.

1012
00:54:20,715 --> 00:54:22,092
It's over. Forget it.

1013
00:54:22,175 --> 00:54:23,969
Now that one's going to be trouble.

1014
00:54:24,052 --> 00:54:25,512
Look at his little face.

1015
00:54:25,595 --> 00:54:27,681
Little rascal.
Come here, you little rascal.

1016
00:54:27,764 --> 00:54:31,601
Come here, honey.
Come here, you little rascal.

1017
00:54:31,685 --> 00:54:33,687
Come here. God, he threw everything.

1018
00:54:35,063 --> 00:54:37,857
You're going to be trouble,
because you're a little rascal.

1019
00:54:39,526 --> 00:54:41,528
-Dad?
-Oh! Hi, guys.

1020
00:54:41,611 --> 00:54:43,571
-Daddy!
-God, I missed you, my loves.

1021
00:54:43,655 --> 00:54:45,615
Careful with Daddy's arm, it hurts.

1022
00:54:47,033 --> 00:54:48,660
-How are you?
-Oh, Dad.

1023
00:54:48,743 --> 00:54:51,663
This is Brenda, Simone's niece.

1024
00:54:51,746 --> 00:54:54,833
-She can come every day, okay?
-Yeah, Dad, she's really cool.

1025
00:54:54,916 --> 00:54:56,710
Dad, seriously, she's really cool.

1026
00:54:56,793 --> 00:54:59,045
-Thank you.
-And what were you doing just now?

1027
00:54:59,129 --> 00:55:00,338
-Just so I know.
-Now?

1028
00:55:00,422 --> 00:55:03,341
-Yeah.
-We were… We were studying math.

1029
00:55:03,425 --> 00:55:04,759
-Yeah!
-Square root of eight.

1030
00:55:04,843 --> 00:55:05,885
-Right?
-Yes.

1031
00:55:05,969 --> 00:55:07,053
A new Pythagoras thing.

1032
00:55:07,137 --> 00:55:09,931
And João asked me to help him
with the obscene triangle.

1033
00:55:10,015 --> 00:55:12,058
No, I mean, the Bermuda Triangle.

1034
00:55:12,142 --> 00:55:13,893
-Did you ask that?
-I did.

1035
00:55:13,977 --> 00:55:15,603
-Right?
-Playground.

1036
00:55:15,687 --> 00:55:17,314
-Playground?
-What did he say?

1037
00:55:17,397 --> 00:55:20,900
Do you want to go
to the playground? Playground!

1038
00:55:21,401 --> 00:55:23,528
Bye, people!
We're going to the playground.

1039
00:55:23,611 --> 00:55:24,779
-Bye, guys!
-Bye!

1040
00:55:24,863 --> 00:55:27,490
Playground!

1041
00:55:27,574 --> 00:55:29,701
See? She understands what he says.

1042
00:55:38,084 --> 00:55:40,086
-Mr. Fred. Excuse me.
-Hey, Brenda.

1043
00:55:40,170 --> 00:55:43,298
I'm sorry if I did anything wrong.
I joke around like that for fun.

1044
00:55:43,381 --> 00:55:45,425
The kids like it.
It keeps them entertained.

1045
00:55:45,508 --> 00:55:47,844
Don't worry, it was great.
Let me ask you something.

1046
00:55:47,927 --> 00:55:50,722
What kind of work did you do before?
Just so I know.

1047
00:55:50,805 --> 00:55:51,973
-Me?
-Yes.

1048
00:55:52,057 --> 00:55:54,851
I worked at a garment factory,
on the administrative side.

1049
00:55:54,934 --> 00:55:56,728
I worked with numbers and all that.

1050
00:55:56,811 --> 00:55:59,105
And I left
because something better came up.

1051
00:55:59,189 --> 00:56:00,732
At a friend's cake factory.

1052
00:56:00,815 --> 00:56:02,984
She wanted me there
because of my experience.

1053
00:56:03,068 --> 00:56:06,571
I went to work with her, it worked out,
but now I'm taking it easy

1054
00:56:06,654 --> 00:56:08,573
because I want to go back to college.

1055
00:56:08,656 --> 00:56:10,575
I'll be honest with you.

1056
00:56:10,658 --> 00:56:13,870
My dream, my real dream in life,
is to own my own publishing house.

1057
00:56:13,953 --> 00:56:15,580
-Oh, that's so cool.
-Yeah.

1058
00:56:15,663 --> 00:56:18,166
-I want to be a translator.
-That's great. Really great.

1059
00:56:19,042 --> 00:56:20,752
-It's nice, right?
-Very cool.

1060
00:56:22,253 --> 00:56:23,421
So, that's it, Mr. Fred.

1061
00:56:23,505 --> 00:56:26,508
I think I should go,
or I'll get stuck in traffic.

1062
00:56:26,591 --> 00:56:28,426
-Yes. I'll walk you out.
-So I better go.

1063
00:56:28,510 --> 00:56:29,886
-Thank you.
-Before you leave,

1064
00:56:29,969 --> 00:56:32,722
can you give me the number
for your friend's cake factory?

1065
00:56:32,806 --> 00:56:34,599
Because I had an idea.

1066
00:56:34,682 --> 00:56:37,644
I can pick up some cake for the kids.
They'll love it.

1067
00:56:37,727 --> 00:56:39,854
-The friend I said I worked for?
-Yeah.

1068
00:56:40,438 --> 00:56:42,899
It's closed, Mr. Fred.
The pandemic, you know?

1069
00:56:42,982 --> 00:56:44,109
-It's closed.
-I see.

1070
00:56:44,192 --> 00:56:45,944
-What a shame.
-Okay. See you soon.

1071
00:56:46,027 --> 00:56:48,363
Thank you for everything. It was great.

1072
00:56:49,489 --> 00:56:50,824
-Mr. Fred.
-Yes.

1073
00:56:50,907 --> 00:56:52,367
-I'm sorry, Mr. Fred.
-Sorry?

1074
00:56:52,450 --> 00:56:54,369
I didn't mean to lie to you, but I did.

1075
00:56:54,452 --> 00:56:55,954
-What?
-I lied, Mr. Fred.

1076
00:56:56,037 --> 00:56:59,416
What I just told you was actually
more of an idealized version of things.

1077
00:56:59,499 --> 00:57:02,210
It's what I dreamed of being in life.

1078
00:57:02,293 --> 00:57:05,171
What I really am is someone
who bounces from job to job.

1079
00:57:05,255 --> 00:57:07,257
-That's okay.
-The last one was last week.

1080
00:57:07,340 --> 00:57:09,300
They fired me
because of three wing screws.

1081
00:57:09,384 --> 00:57:10,844
Can you believe it?

1082
00:57:12,011 --> 00:57:13,596
-Three wing screws?
-Yes.

1083
00:57:14,848 --> 00:57:17,350
-Where?
-Rabbit Home Center, do you know it?

1084
00:57:17,434 --> 00:57:19,894
-No.
-Mr. Fred, that place is horrible.

1085
00:57:19,978 --> 00:57:22,188
Honestly, I can't stand rabbits anymore.

1086
00:57:22,272 --> 00:57:23,606
-The animal rabbit!
-Yes.

1087
00:57:23,690 --> 00:57:25,984
I'm triggered.
I don't know how Easter is gonna be.

1088
00:57:26,067 --> 00:57:28,820
If I see a rabbit, Mr. Fred,
I might punch it.

1089
00:57:28,903 --> 00:57:32,407
-The rabbit and the man that fired me.
-Wait a second. It's okay, come here.

1090
00:57:32,490 --> 00:57:34,492
Follow me. Take a seat, please.

1091
00:57:34,576 --> 00:57:37,370
Do you, by any chance,
know the guy that fired you?

1092
00:57:37,454 --> 00:57:38,580
Of course not, Mr. Fred.

1093
00:57:38,663 --> 00:57:41,749
If I knew the man who fired me,
he wouldn't be alive anymore!

1094
00:57:41,833 --> 00:57:43,251
-Calm down.
-He wouldn't.

1095
00:57:43,334 --> 00:57:45,295
I would grab him, sit him down,

1096
00:57:45,378 --> 00:57:48,173
grab a pair of tweezers,
and pull out every hair on his body,

1097
00:57:48,256 --> 00:57:49,257
nice and slow.

1098
00:57:53,052 --> 00:57:54,888
Why did you steal? You stole!

1099
00:57:54,971 --> 00:57:57,140
I was going to buy it,
but when I got to work,

1100
00:57:57,223 --> 00:57:59,976
can you believe a box
with 100 wings screws fell on my head?

1101
00:58:00,059 --> 00:58:02,604
I was honest.
I should have stolen all 100.

1102
00:58:02,687 --> 00:58:05,565
I only stole three,
there were 97 left in the box.

1103
00:58:05,648 --> 00:58:06,691
-Was that fair?
-No.

1104
00:58:06,774 --> 00:58:09,194
For them to fire me like that,
kick me to the curb?

1105
00:58:09,277 --> 00:58:11,946
-Never.
-They fired me and gave me nothing.

1106
00:58:12,030 --> 00:58:14,824
That place is bad.
They treat the employees so poorly.

1107
00:58:14,908 --> 00:58:16,326
-You have no idea.
-Yes.

1108
00:58:16,409 --> 00:58:17,827
They screw us so much.

1109
00:58:17,911 --> 00:58:20,455
If we don't screw them a little,
we'll go crazy.

1110
00:58:20,538 --> 00:58:22,540
But did you do that before? Steal?

1111
00:58:22,624 --> 00:58:24,417
Of course not, Mr. Fred. No way.

1112
00:58:24,501 --> 00:58:27,420
For God's sake, I was just launching
this personality trait.

1113
00:58:27,504 --> 00:58:29,714
-Oh, okay.
-Where do you work?

1114
00:58:30,590 --> 00:58:33,092
-You're a lawyer, right?
-Me?

1115
00:58:33,176 --> 00:58:34,469
Yeah, you're a lawyer.

1116
00:58:35,053 --> 00:58:36,012
I am.

1117
00:58:37,096 --> 00:58:40,183
I knew you were, because I saw
so many law books upstairs.

1118
00:58:40,266 --> 00:58:41,935
-In the office.
-That's right.

1119
00:58:42,936 --> 00:58:45,313
-Mr. Fred, I have to go, okay?
-Hm-hmm.

1120
00:58:45,396 --> 00:58:48,566
-But I'll be back tomorrow.
-Sure.

1121
00:58:48,650 --> 00:58:49,692
-Okay?
-I'll be waiting.

1122
00:58:49,776 --> 00:58:51,069
-If you need anything…
-Sure.

1123
00:58:51,861 --> 00:58:53,488
Article 93, huh?

1124
00:59:03,915 --> 00:59:06,334
Honey, Tom Tom just fell asleep.
Come here.

1125
00:59:08,753 --> 00:59:11,214
About that thing,
Daddy researched everything.

1126
00:59:11,297 --> 00:59:13,675
I already talked to Brenda.
She told me everything.

1127
00:59:13,758 --> 00:59:16,386
Brenda? I'm glad you brought her up.

1128
00:59:16,469 --> 00:59:18,721
Don't you think Brenda
seems a little strange?

1129
00:59:18,805 --> 00:59:20,932
Because Dad can think
of other options, okay?

1130
00:59:21,015 --> 00:59:23,393
Dad, if you fire Brenda,
I'll learn how to drive

1131
00:59:23,476 --> 00:59:24,978
and run you over, okay?

1132
00:59:25,061 --> 00:59:28,189
-Jesus, honey, Dad just thought--
-No, Dad.

1133
00:59:28,273 --> 00:59:29,774
Give Daddy a kiss…

1134
00:59:39,200 --> 00:59:40,493
Thank you, son.

1135
00:59:41,202 --> 00:59:43,288
Mr. Fred!

1136
00:59:46,666 --> 00:59:48,585
The girls' snacks, you almost forgot.

1137
00:59:48,668 --> 00:59:51,254
Thank you so much. You're wonderful.

1138
00:59:51,337 --> 00:59:53,631
-Thank you.
-No worries.

1139
00:59:53,715 --> 00:59:55,091
Have a good day at school.

1140
00:59:55,174 --> 00:59:57,218
Here, girls, your snacks. Thank you.

1141
00:59:57,302 --> 00:59:58,595
You're lovely.

1142
01:00:01,472 --> 01:00:02,473
Geez.

1143
01:00:02,974 --> 01:00:05,310
WELCOME!
RABBIT HOME CENTER

1144
01:00:05,393 --> 01:00:06,394
ENTRY

1145
01:00:10,565 --> 01:00:12,650
-Mr. Fred!
-Jesus, what the heck?

1146
01:00:12,734 --> 01:00:14,193
-Beth?
-Come here!

1147
01:00:14,277 --> 01:00:15,778
You look like you're on stakeout.

1148
01:00:15,862 --> 01:00:17,780
-Come.
-Couldn't you wait?

1149
01:00:17,864 --> 01:00:20,325
I'm desperate, Mr. Fred.

1150
01:00:20,408 --> 01:00:21,951
You know that Family Day,

1151
01:00:22,035 --> 01:00:25,121
the company's celebration,
is the day after tomorrow, right?

1152
01:00:25,204 --> 01:00:26,581
I know, Beth, but look,

1153
01:00:26,664 --> 01:00:27,874
Roberta is not home,

1154
01:00:27,957 --> 01:00:30,043
my kids won't want to come,
I won't force them,

1155
01:00:30,126 --> 01:00:32,920
and I don't know if you heard,
but I fell off the balcony.

1156
01:00:34,172 --> 01:00:37,216
Okay, Mr. Fred,
but the whole Board is going.

1157
01:00:37,300 --> 01:00:40,970
Mr. Dante and his entire family
will be there.

1158
01:00:41,721 --> 01:00:44,015
You know those margarine commercials

1159
01:00:44,098 --> 01:00:47,310
with a mom who looks like a model
and two beautiful kids

1160
01:00:47,393 --> 01:00:49,979
whose bright smiles are so white
it could blind you?

1161
01:00:50,938 --> 01:00:53,691
That's Mr. Dante's family.
They look like TV stars.

1162
01:00:54,442 --> 01:00:56,611
{\an8}Look what he did to get everyone excited.

1163
01:00:56,694 --> 01:00:58,446
{\an8}You better bring your kids.

1164
01:00:58,529 --> 01:01:02,241
{\an8}I was going to send it to you,
but I thought it was better if you came.

1165
01:01:03,368 --> 01:01:07,705
To see it in person. Who knows,
maybe you'll bump into Mr. Pontes.

1166
01:01:07,789 --> 01:01:10,291
The more you're seen,
the harder you are to forget.

1167
01:01:10,375 --> 01:01:11,834
Beth, for the love of God,

1168
01:01:11,918 --> 01:01:14,629
I've only been gone a few days.
Nobody's forgotten me yet.

1169
01:01:17,131 --> 01:01:18,383
You think?

1170
01:01:18,466 --> 01:01:19,884
It's just that some people

1171
01:01:19,967 --> 01:01:23,513
only have to be gone for a little while
to be forgotten.

1172
01:01:27,517 --> 01:01:29,769
<i>You better bring your children.</i>

1173
01:01:32,855 --> 01:01:36,484
So, you're here
because she's there with Tom Tom.

1174
01:01:36,567 --> 01:01:37,568
Exactly.

1175
01:01:38,277 --> 01:01:41,698
And you were the one
who fired her from here?

1176
01:01:41,781 --> 01:01:42,782
Exactly.

1177
01:01:43,783 --> 01:01:46,494
And she doesn't know who you are?

1178
01:01:46,577 --> 01:01:48,996
Exactly. In other words,
I'm sleeping with the enemy.

1179
01:01:49,956 --> 01:01:52,458
No, she is.
She's the one who lost her job,

1180
01:01:52,542 --> 01:01:53,960
she's the one who got fired,

1181
01:01:54,043 --> 01:01:55,586
you're the villain.

1182
01:01:55,670 --> 01:01:57,630
-Come on, man.
-What?

1183
01:01:58,756 --> 01:01:59,757
Pontes.

1184
01:02:02,009 --> 01:02:04,637
-Wait a second.
-Straighten up, man.

1185
01:02:04,721 --> 01:02:05,555
Here.

1186
01:02:06,180 --> 01:02:07,223
Pontes.

1187
01:02:07,306 --> 01:02:08,975
I missed you. I mean, that's not it.

1188
01:02:09,058 --> 01:02:11,310
Thank you for the vacation, because…

1189
01:02:11,394 --> 01:02:14,147
Family Day is coming up, huh?
What a wonderful energy.

1190
01:02:14,230 --> 01:02:15,273
How's everything?

1191
01:02:15,356 --> 01:02:17,734
The planning,
your wonderful wife, how is she?

1192
01:02:17,817 --> 01:02:18,735
She's not well.

1193
01:02:19,402 --> 01:02:20,403
She had a stroke.

1194
01:02:23,364 --> 01:02:24,240
Pontes…

1195
01:02:24,949 --> 01:02:26,075
Man, what the hell?

1196
01:02:26,159 --> 01:02:29,036
Sorry, Pontes is taking time off
because of his wife's health.

1197
01:02:29,120 --> 01:02:32,331
How could you forget to tell me
the most important thing on the planet?

1198
01:02:32,415 --> 01:02:34,751
-My bad, I messed up.
-No, you really did.

1199
01:02:34,834 --> 01:02:37,086
-I know I messed up.
-But you really messed up.

1200
01:02:37,170 --> 01:02:40,506
Fine. I tried to tell you, I tried.

1201
01:02:56,981 --> 01:03:00,318
Guys, look. Dad has many flaws, all right?

1202
01:03:00,401 --> 01:03:03,196
Dad has many flaws, makes mistakes,
but we're here to improve.

1203
01:03:03,279 --> 01:03:04,655
So, what did we do?

1204
01:03:04,739 --> 01:03:07,909
I asked you to write down one thing
that would improve our lives.

1205
01:03:07,992 --> 01:03:09,035
Where is it?

1206
01:03:09,118 --> 01:03:10,578
-I know mine, Dad.
-Really?

1207
01:03:10,661 --> 01:03:12,330
-Yes.
-Everyone know their wishes?

1208
01:03:12,413 --> 01:03:14,957
-Yes.
-We will throw our paper into the fire,

1209
01:03:15,041 --> 01:03:18,461
the fire will go up,
and our lives will get…

1210
01:03:18,544 --> 01:03:21,422
-Better!
-So let's throw them in. One, two, three.

1211
01:03:21,506 --> 01:03:22,757
Come on, Tom Tom, you too.

1212
01:03:23,800 --> 01:03:25,343
Get better, wonderful life!

1213
01:03:25,426 --> 01:03:28,095
Throw it to the universe!

1214
01:03:29,931 --> 01:03:30,890
Yes!

1215
01:03:30,973 --> 01:03:32,683
Guys, I don't want to intrude.

1216
01:03:32,767 --> 01:03:34,101
But what did you ask?

1217
01:03:34,852 --> 01:03:38,940
I asked for love, the end of patriarchy,

1218
01:03:39,023 --> 01:03:41,776
harmony among all people, and world peace.

1219
01:03:42,485 --> 01:03:45,112
That's my wonderful daughter.
I'm proud of you, honey.

1220
01:03:45,196 --> 01:03:46,072
I love you.

1221
01:03:46,155 --> 01:03:48,074
-What about you, son?
-I asked to be rich.

1222
01:03:48,908 --> 01:03:51,536
A practical person.
A person who knows what he wants.

1223
01:03:52,245 --> 01:03:54,914
I'm very proud of you, son.
What about you, Clacla?

1224
01:03:54,997 --> 01:03:56,999
I asked for unity in our family.

1225
01:03:57,083 --> 01:03:58,417
Oh my-- This is for you.

1226
01:03:58,501 --> 01:04:00,545
This is for you. You are wonderful!

1227
01:04:00,628 --> 01:04:05,049
Daddy will tell you what I asked for.
I asked for us to do more things together.

1228
01:04:05,132 --> 01:04:07,260
"But we already do
a lot of things together."

1229
01:04:07,343 --> 01:04:10,346
But a truly united family,
like our ancestors, is always together.

1230
01:04:10,429 --> 01:04:14,767
I asked for us to party together,
go to the movies,

1231
01:04:14,851 --> 01:04:16,811
restaurants, play video games, play ball.

1232
01:04:16,894 --> 01:04:19,146
Maybe to go to Family Day together.
Look at that.

1233
01:04:19,230 --> 01:04:21,816
-Oh no! God forbid.
-No way, I'm not going.

1234
01:04:21,899 --> 01:04:25,570
Guys, Family Day is very important.
All our ancestors have done it.

1235
01:04:25,653 --> 01:04:29,365
We sing to the fire, the forest,
the woods, the moon, the sun.

1236
01:04:29,448 --> 01:04:30,908
Let's do that, guys.

1237
01:04:30,992 --> 01:04:32,368
Let's use our teas,

1238
01:04:32,451 --> 01:04:33,828
our weed!

1239
01:04:33,911 --> 01:04:35,955
-No, not weed. Did I say "weed"?
-Yes.

1240
01:04:36,038 --> 01:04:37,498
-No, not weed.
-I heard it.

1241
01:04:37,582 --> 01:04:40,918
No, honey. I talk to you all day
and you don't ever listen to me.

1242
01:04:41,002 --> 01:04:42,628
When you're not supposed to list--

1243
01:04:42,712 --> 01:04:44,922
-Bye!
-Bye? Honey, no.

1244
01:04:45,006 --> 01:04:47,550
-Excuse me.
-No weed! Keep the fire in your heart.

1245
01:04:49,635 --> 01:04:52,013
Yes, honey, help me out. Look.

1246
01:04:52,096 --> 01:04:54,974
The important thing's
that everyone goes to Family Day.

1247
01:04:55,057 --> 01:04:57,143
<i>Hey, hey, hey</i>
<i>To Family Day</i>

1248
01:04:57,226 --> 01:04:58,936
<i>Hey, hey</i>
<i>To Family Day</i>

1249
01:04:59,020 --> 01:05:00,730
<i>Hey, hey</i>
<i>Convince my siblings</i>

1250
01:05:00,813 --> 01:05:02,398
<i>Hey, hey</i>
<i>To Family Day</i>

1251
01:05:02,481 --> 01:05:03,608
<i>Convince my siblings</i>

1252
01:05:03,691 --> 01:05:04,859
Yes!

1253
01:05:04,942 --> 01:05:07,236
-<i>To Family Day!</i>
-Let's go to Family Day!

1254
01:05:07,320 --> 01:05:08,529
Let's go! Fire!

1255
01:05:09,196 --> 01:05:10,990
Heading to the fire of love!

1256
01:05:14,118 --> 01:05:17,121
If you don't want to think about Dad,
who does everything for you,

1257
01:05:17,204 --> 01:05:18,623
think about yourselves.

1258
01:05:18,706 --> 01:05:21,834
This company pays for our life.
You need to go to Family Day.

1259
01:05:22,418 --> 01:05:25,171
Okay. If you can say
three things that I like,

1260
01:05:25,254 --> 01:05:26,297
I'll go.

1261
01:05:26,380 --> 01:05:29,926
Honey, that's easy.
You like ice cream, pizza,

1262
01:05:30,593 --> 01:05:32,094
and boys.

1263
01:05:34,221 --> 01:05:35,556
Are you a lesbian, honey?

1264
01:05:35,640 --> 01:05:37,391
Daddy will love you just the same.

1265
01:05:37,475 --> 01:05:39,685
-This is amazing.
-Ugh, Dad!

1266
01:05:39,769 --> 01:05:42,104
Three things I like.

1267
01:05:42,188 --> 01:05:43,147
Me specifically.

1268
01:05:50,071 --> 01:05:50,988
Come on, honey.

1269
01:05:53,991 --> 01:05:55,534
Grapes, honey. Grapes!

1270
01:05:57,203 --> 01:05:59,330
Son, didn't you ask to be rich?

1271
01:05:59,413 --> 01:06:01,791
The thing at the fire blew up.
Feels like a bad omen.

1272
01:06:01,874 --> 01:06:04,543
If I lose this job,
boom, we're poor immediately.

1273
01:06:04,627 --> 01:06:06,545
But if we crush it on Family Day,

1274
01:06:06,629 --> 01:06:09,090
that's success, a promotion, money.

1275
01:06:09,173 --> 01:06:11,968
We'll get closer to what you asked for,
my wonderful son.

1276
01:06:12,051 --> 01:06:13,427
Great, Dad.

1277
01:06:13,511 --> 01:06:16,681
But if I go,
I want to throw a party here at home.

1278
01:06:17,515 --> 01:06:18,599
-Who?
-Me.

1279
01:06:20,851 --> 01:06:23,396
-Are you blackmailing me?
-Oh my God.

1280
01:06:23,479 --> 01:06:24,939
Are you becoming a bad person?

1281
01:06:25,856 --> 01:06:26,941
So, I'm not going.

1282
01:06:27,024 --> 01:06:28,192
You're a bad person!

1283
01:06:30,987 --> 01:06:32,405
My son became a bad person.

1284
01:06:32,905 --> 01:06:34,824
My son became a bad person.

1285
01:06:37,243 --> 01:06:41,163
Cecília, thank you. Everything you said
is super useful for my research.

1286
01:06:41,247 --> 01:06:44,291
This is going to be wonderful.
I don't even know how to thank you.

1287
01:06:44,375 --> 01:06:46,794
-You're wonderful.
-Thank you.

1288
01:06:47,753 --> 01:06:49,714
-I'll email you.
-Okay.

1289
01:06:49,797 --> 01:06:51,590
-I'll be waiting. Thanks.
-Okay.

1290
01:06:54,719 --> 01:06:55,636
What is it, Beta?

1291
01:06:55,720 --> 01:06:57,763
I'm so happy to be here with you.

1292
01:06:57,847 --> 01:07:00,266
To watch you working.
Work is so important, right?

1293
01:07:00,349 --> 01:07:02,393
It's so good to do what we love, right?

1294
01:07:02,476 --> 01:07:04,729
-Yes!
-Wow, that was very cool.

1295
01:07:04,812 --> 01:07:06,397
I was nervous. Did you see?

1296
01:07:06,480 --> 01:07:09,692
No. You were nervous?
You looked so confident.

1297
01:07:09,775 --> 01:07:11,944
-Yeah?
-You were articulate. Wonderful.

1298
01:07:12,028 --> 01:07:13,738
I'm so glad you were here, sis.

1299
01:07:13,821 --> 01:07:15,364
-It was beautiful.
-Thank you.

1300
01:07:15,448 --> 01:07:17,867
-I'm still cold.
-Come on, take a sip.

1301
01:07:17,950 --> 01:07:19,410
-For the love of God.
-Go.

1302
01:07:19,493 --> 01:07:21,495
-Can you order another one?
-Yes. Excuse me?

1303
01:07:21,579 --> 01:07:22,621
Two more.

1304
01:07:27,168 --> 01:07:28,836
I'll go to Family Day.

1305
01:07:30,379 --> 01:07:31,422
You can thank Brenda.

1306
01:07:36,510 --> 01:07:37,595
Brenda?

1307
01:07:38,179 --> 01:07:39,472
Why do I have to sweep--

1308
01:07:39,555 --> 01:07:40,681
-Brenda?
-Yes.

1309
01:07:40,765 --> 01:07:44,018
How did you pull off the miracle
of getting her to go to Family Day?

1310
01:07:44,101 --> 01:07:46,479
Look, Mr. Fred,
I'm not trying to be annoying.

1311
01:07:46,562 --> 01:07:49,690
But we have those words in Portuguese.
<i>Dia da Família.</i>

1312
01:07:49,774 --> 01:07:52,193
-Yeah. But what did you do?
-Just so you know.

1313
01:07:52,276 --> 01:07:54,320
-It was simple.
-What do you mean, simple?

1314
01:07:54,403 --> 01:07:55,821
Nothing about that is simple.

1315
01:07:55,905 --> 01:07:58,282
To say it's simple is humiliating.
What did you do?

1316
01:07:58,365 --> 01:08:00,826
I just had to tell her
that it was important to you.

1317
01:08:01,994 --> 01:08:02,828
Yeah.

1318
01:08:02,912 --> 01:08:04,997
Are you serious? Brenda, thank you.

1319
01:08:05,081 --> 01:08:08,334
-No problem.
-I don't even know how to thank you.

1320
01:08:08,918 --> 01:08:10,711
-Thank you so much.
-That's it.

1321
01:08:10,795 --> 01:08:13,380
Mr. Fred, come here.
Let me tell you something quick.

1322
01:08:13,464 --> 01:08:15,216
-Yes.
-Since you're here.

1323
01:08:15,299 --> 01:08:17,134
You said you don't know how to thank me.

1324
01:08:17,218 --> 01:08:18,469
-Right?
-Right.

1325
01:08:18,552 --> 01:08:21,263
Yeah, but I know.
Mr. Fred, here's the thing.

1326
01:08:21,347 --> 01:08:24,642
If you really want to help me,
let's sue the Rabbit Home Center?

1327
01:08:24,725 --> 01:08:28,229
Since you're a lawyer,
you can help me sue them, you know?

1328
01:08:28,312 --> 01:08:29,688
A tip, as a lawyer.

1329
01:08:29,772 --> 01:08:31,982
Revenge doesn't work.
Forget about it, Brenda.

1330
01:08:32,066 --> 01:08:33,400
It's bad for your health.

1331
01:08:33,484 --> 01:08:35,319
-Judges don't like that.
-Mr. Fred.

1332
01:08:35,402 --> 01:08:38,322
I don't want to be annoying,
but I have to say this.

1333
01:08:38,405 --> 01:08:40,407
-I'm not being rude. It's not revenge.
-Sure.

1334
01:08:40,491 --> 01:08:42,785
It's not. I know,
I've heard this advice before.

1335
01:08:42,868 --> 01:08:44,662
-Revenge gave my mom an ulcer.
-See?

1336
01:08:44,745 --> 01:08:46,747
It's about justice, Mr. Fred.

1337
01:08:46,831 --> 01:08:49,416
Justice has a new name now,
it's called revenge? No.

1338
01:08:49,500 --> 01:08:51,627
It's justice.
What they did to me was wrong.

1339
01:08:51,710 --> 01:08:53,379
-What they did was very wrong.
-Yes.

1340
01:08:53,462 --> 01:08:55,840
You need to see my termination papers.
They're awful!

1341
01:08:55,923 --> 01:09:00,136
And if justice fails, let me tell you,
then I'll go looking for revenge.

1342
01:09:00,219 --> 01:09:02,304
I'll go after the bastard
who did this to me.

1343
01:09:02,388 --> 01:09:04,473
-I'll get him. I'll find…
-For the love of God.

1344
01:09:04,557 --> 01:09:07,309
-I'll help you!
-You'll help me, Mr. Fred?

1345
01:09:07,393 --> 01:09:09,353
-Are you serious?
-I'll help you. Of course.

1346
01:09:09,436 --> 01:09:11,313
My God, Mr. Fred. I'm getting emotional.

1347
01:09:11,397 --> 01:09:13,482
-There's no need.
-You are a good man!

1348
01:09:13,566 --> 01:09:15,693
You are a great man. Thank you so much.

1349
01:09:15,776 --> 01:09:19,905
Look, I even brought my ID
so you can take care of this for me.

1350
01:09:19,989 --> 01:09:21,407
When can you help me?

1351
01:09:28,998 --> 01:09:31,125
WELCOME

1352
01:09:36,964 --> 01:09:38,465
Mr. Fred, you're still at home?

1353
01:09:38,549 --> 01:09:40,968
Beth, look,
people with kids are never on time.

1354
01:09:41,051 --> 01:09:44,138
In fact, people don't even expect
parents to be on time.

1355
01:09:44,221 --> 01:09:46,348
Jesus Christ,
where are my car keys? Again.

1356
01:09:46,432 --> 01:09:49,101
Malu, Clacla, get ready,
for the love of God, Daddy's late.

1357
01:09:49,185 --> 01:09:50,102
Is Dante there?

1358
01:09:50,186 --> 01:09:51,979
His whole family is here.

1359
01:09:52,062 --> 01:09:53,564
His wife, his kids.

1360
01:09:53,647 --> 01:09:56,734
<i>So get ready, Mr. Fred,</i>
<i>for the love of God.</i>

1361
01:09:56,817 --> 01:09:58,152
<i>And hurry up.</i>

1362
01:09:58,235 --> 01:10:02,656
RABBIT HOME CENTER
24TH FAMILY DAY

1363
01:10:19,965 --> 01:10:22,885
-I swear I'll give it back.
-Guys, I found my keys.

1364
01:10:24,845 --> 01:10:26,597
It was here the whole-- Huh?

1365
01:10:26,680 --> 01:10:28,682
Brenda? I thought you were off today.

1366
01:10:28,766 --> 01:10:31,060
Mr. Fred, I forgot my ID.

1367
01:10:31,143 --> 01:10:33,604
-It's okay, we'll find it.
-Okay, thanks.

1368
01:10:33,687 --> 01:10:36,357
I also lose a lot of stuff
running around here. Come here.

1369
01:10:37,566 --> 01:10:39,652
-Sometimes they're here.
-Excuse me.

1370
01:10:39,735 --> 01:10:41,737
-Sometimes they're in the drawer.
-Mm-hmm.

1371
01:10:44,823 --> 01:10:46,700
-What's this?
-What?

1372
01:10:48,744 --> 01:10:51,372
This is gorgeous, Mr. Fred.

1373
01:10:51,455 --> 01:10:53,374
-Is it your wife's?
-Yes, it is.

1374
01:10:53,457 --> 01:10:55,584
-Aunt Simone says she has great taste.
-Yes.

1375
01:10:55,668 --> 01:10:56,752
I love it.

1376
01:10:57,378 --> 01:10:59,380
She has great taste
and she's a lot of fun.

1377
01:10:59,463 --> 01:11:01,799
-You'll love her.
-I will, I'm sure.

1378
01:11:01,882 --> 01:11:04,009
Let me check these drawers too.

1379
01:11:04,093 --> 01:11:05,427
-Okay.
-All right?

1380
01:11:05,511 --> 01:11:08,013
I'm so excited to sue them, Mr. Fred.

1381
01:11:08,097 --> 01:11:10,724
The Rabbit Home Center people.
They're such bad people.

1382
01:11:10,808 --> 01:11:14,228
They don't appreciate us.
But this time, they will. You know why?

1383
01:11:14,311 --> 01:11:15,312
Compensation!

1384
01:11:17,982 --> 01:11:20,317
Found it! Brenda, I found your ID.

1385
01:11:24,280 --> 01:11:25,781
Where do you work?

1386
01:11:27,533 --> 01:11:29,660
What do you mean by "where"?
Because where…

1387
01:11:29,743 --> 01:11:31,453
Do you mean the neighborhood?

1388
01:11:31,537 --> 01:11:32,579
What?

1389
01:11:32,663 --> 01:11:36,750
-Do you work at the Rabbit Home Center?
-Calm down, okay? Breathe.

1390
01:11:36,834 --> 01:11:38,335
Let's be civil, it's all right.

1391
01:11:38,419 --> 01:11:42,172
Did you think it was fair to fire me
for three screws out of a box of 100?

1392
01:11:43,299 --> 01:11:44,174
Brenda, you stole.

1393
01:11:45,050 --> 01:11:47,094
I-- They-- They pressured me.

1394
01:11:47,177 --> 01:11:50,889
How were you going to be my lawyer?
Were you going to sue yourself?

1395
01:11:51,682 --> 01:11:53,058
I'm not even a lawyer.

1396
01:11:53,642 --> 01:11:56,645
Look, not everyone has
the same opportunities, okay?

1397
01:11:57,229 --> 01:12:00,524
Not everyone gets a second,
third, or fourth chance.

1398
01:12:00,607 --> 01:12:04,611
Not everyone has the privilege
of not being cut off after one mistake.

1399
01:12:04,695 --> 01:12:07,740
I think you're not considering

1400
01:12:07,823 --> 01:12:09,908
the fact that you committed a crime.

1401
01:12:11,076 --> 01:12:14,496
-You stole, Brenda.
-Three screws from a million-dollar store.

1402
01:12:14,580 --> 01:12:15,914
I was making minimum wage.

1403
01:12:15,998 --> 01:12:19,960
It's not about the number of screws,
Brenda, it's about character.

1404
01:12:20,044 --> 01:12:21,503
-Character?
-Character.

1405
01:12:22,421 --> 01:12:24,798
Look, Mr. Fred, I quit.

1406
01:12:24,882 --> 01:12:26,425
-Huh?
-I quit.

1407
01:12:27,426 --> 01:12:28,510
I'm leaving.

1408
01:12:28,594 --> 01:12:31,138
I won't give you the satisfaction
of firing me twice.

1409
01:12:31,221 --> 01:12:33,640
I'm out,
but this time it's because I want to.

1410
01:12:49,907 --> 01:12:52,368
How could he fire Brenda?

1411
01:12:52,451 --> 01:12:54,453
-I know.
-He's coming.

1412
01:12:58,207 --> 01:12:59,083
What?

1413
01:13:00,209 --> 01:13:01,126
I changed my mind.

1414
01:13:02,211 --> 01:13:05,381
<i>So we are a family</i>
<i>We're going to Family Day</i>

1415
01:13:05,964 --> 01:13:08,592
How nice, you guys.
This is going to be fun.

1416
01:13:09,510 --> 01:13:11,053
It's gonna be peace and love.

1417
01:13:20,521 --> 01:13:23,857
That's right, everyone.
It's our Family Day!

1418
01:13:26,652 --> 01:13:29,655
-And now it's time for our mascot…
-Hey, let's go, guys.

1419
01:13:29,738 --> 01:13:33,617
…to light the Rabbit Home Center's
Family Olympics

1420
01:13:33,700 --> 01:13:35,577
and warm our hearts.

1421
01:13:35,661 --> 01:13:39,998
-Let's go. Three, two, one.
-Rabbit, rabbit!

1422
01:13:40,082 --> 01:13:41,917
Rabbit, rabbit!

1423
01:13:42,000 --> 01:13:44,420
That's it, may the best one win!

1424
01:13:46,672 --> 01:13:47,923
There you go.

1425
01:13:48,006 --> 01:13:51,802
The Rabbit Home Center Games
are officially open!

1426
01:13:54,721 --> 01:13:56,056
Go, Fred!

1427
01:13:57,474 --> 01:13:59,977
-Red!
-Red!

1428
01:14:00,060 --> 01:14:01,979
Hold on, wait a second.

1429
01:14:02,062 --> 01:14:03,730
-Go, Dad!
-Brazil's defense!

1430
01:14:07,109 --> 01:14:08,861
Hold the horns, man!

1431
01:14:11,697 --> 01:14:15,742
-Yellow!
-Yellow!

1432
01:14:23,041 --> 01:14:25,252
-Yellow!
-Yellow!

1433
01:14:25,335 --> 01:14:26,503
He won't let go.

1434
01:14:26,587 --> 01:14:31,425
And the yellow team scores another point!

1435
01:14:31,508 --> 01:14:33,719
Red team just couldn't
make it happen this time.

1436
01:14:36,430 --> 01:14:41,059
The rivalry between the red team
and the yellow team is heating up.

1437
01:14:41,143 --> 01:14:43,061
-Pull!
-For the love of God, go!

1438
01:14:43,145 --> 01:14:45,147
-Go!
-Go!

1439
01:14:45,230 --> 01:14:47,357
-No way!
-Go, Dad!

1440
01:14:47,441 --> 01:14:50,194
-Pull!
-Go!

1441
01:14:50,277 --> 01:14:51,612
No!

1442
01:14:56,533 --> 01:14:59,745
The yellow team scores!

1443
01:14:59,828 --> 01:15:04,249
-Yellow!
-Yellow!

1444
01:15:04,833 --> 01:15:05,834
Look at that.

1445
01:15:07,669 --> 01:15:08,670
Perfect.

1446
01:15:10,589 --> 01:15:13,634
That's awesome.
Didn't you want us to come, Dad?

1447
01:15:13,717 --> 01:15:17,554
-It's our only chance to win.
-Yeah, and it's worth more points.

1448
01:15:17,638 --> 01:15:19,223
-Are you going, Beth?
-No.

1449
01:15:19,306 --> 01:15:22,643
{\an8}Twenty points for the yellow team,
ten for the red team.

1450
01:15:23,352 --> 01:15:26,563
-Yellow!
-Suck it, red!

1451
01:15:28,524 --> 01:15:30,192
Hold him for me, please.

1452
01:15:38,575 --> 01:15:40,202
Guys, please, aim for the middle.

1453
01:15:40,285 --> 01:15:42,621
-One mistake can be fatal.
-Ready?

1454
01:15:42,704 --> 01:15:45,707
Yes, but don't ask me again,
because I might regret it, my love.

1455
01:15:45,791 --> 01:15:47,584
Dad, we need to tell you something.

1456
01:15:47,668 --> 01:15:49,586
Honey, I love you all very much too.

1457
01:15:49,670 --> 01:15:51,088
-It's not that.
-What is it?

1458
01:15:51,713 --> 01:15:55,300
It was good that Mom went on that trip.
We got to know each other better.

1459
01:15:55,384 --> 01:15:58,220
That's so beautiful,
Daddy loves you very much too, okay?

1460
01:15:58,303 --> 01:16:00,347
But we didn't like what we saw.

1461
01:16:00,430 --> 01:16:03,517
-What?
-And we think you should go on a trip too.

1462
01:16:03,600 --> 01:16:04,768
-Yeah.
-Right?

1463
01:16:04,851 --> 01:16:07,688
Guys, stop, get me out of here. Sir!

1464
01:16:07,771 --> 01:16:09,982
I want out. Where's Beth?
Tom Tom might need me.

1465
01:16:10,065 --> 01:16:12,150
-You don't even understand him.
-But if I did,

1466
01:16:12,234 --> 01:16:15,696
he'd probably be saying, "Dad,
get out of there, it's too dangerous."

1467
01:16:15,779 --> 01:16:18,282
He'd tell you to hold on tight, Dad.

1468
01:16:18,365 --> 01:16:20,867
-Just like a wing screw.
-Huh?

1469
01:16:21,743 --> 01:16:23,120
No.

1470
01:16:23,203 --> 01:16:25,330
No. You've become a bad person, son.

1471
01:16:25,414 --> 01:16:28,667
Look, say "bye" to Daddy, he's gonna roll.

1472
01:16:28,750 --> 01:16:30,586
No. Who are you?

1473
01:16:31,295 --> 01:16:34,840
What kind of kids are you? No!

1474
01:16:34,923 --> 01:16:37,175
I can't believe you're doing this!

1475
01:17:11,293 --> 01:17:14,379
I can't believe it! Jesus, help me!

1476
01:17:29,102 --> 01:17:30,854
Help!

1477
01:17:37,944 --> 01:17:38,945
The rabbit!

1478
01:17:39,613 --> 01:17:42,908
-Didn't we overdo it?
-Help!

1479
01:17:42,991 --> 01:17:44,284
Probably.

1480
01:17:46,411 --> 01:17:48,413
Oh my God. What are you doing, man?

1481
01:17:48,497 --> 01:17:50,749
-Just a second.
-Give me your hand. I'll help you.

1482
01:17:50,832 --> 01:17:53,377
-Are you insane? Hold my hand.
-Take me out of here.

1483
01:17:53,460 --> 01:17:54,711
Fred…

1484
01:17:54,795 --> 01:17:57,297
-Wait a second, I'll-- Hold this.
-Wait.

1485
01:17:57,381 --> 01:17:59,675
Wait, I can't see. Wait!

1486
01:18:02,761 --> 01:18:03,720
My God.

1487
01:18:08,517 --> 01:18:10,310
Help! My tail is on fire.

1488
01:18:10,394 --> 01:18:13,772
-Fred, do something.
-Calm down, Mr. Pontes. Calm down!

1489
01:18:13,855 --> 01:18:16,650
-Do something, fix this mess! What?
-Calm down!

1490
01:18:22,531 --> 01:18:23,782
Run, people. Run!

1491
01:18:24,950 --> 01:18:27,869
-Run!
-Somebody help me! It's real fire!

1492
01:18:27,953 --> 01:18:29,871
I don't wanna die!

1493
01:18:30,414 --> 01:18:33,333
Help, people, help!

1494
01:18:35,127 --> 01:18:36,128
Water!

1495
01:18:42,718 --> 01:18:48,181
RABBIT HOME CENTER
24TH FAMILY DAY

1496
01:19:22,549 --> 01:19:24,843
Yeah, Tom Tom.

1497
01:20:24,277 --> 01:20:25,654
-You can go.
-Can I go?

1498
01:20:32,244 --> 01:20:33,286
Excuse me…

1499
01:20:36,414 --> 01:20:37,791
You can go, Daddy.

1500
01:20:37,874 --> 01:20:40,710
-Can I? Can I go?
-Mm-hmm. You're free to go.

1501
01:20:41,753 --> 01:20:44,714
Bye, Tom Tom. Bye, son.

1502
01:20:45,882 --> 01:20:48,176
-He's fine, right?
-Yes. Go.

1503
01:20:52,514 --> 01:20:54,641
Yeah. That's right.

1504
01:20:54,724 --> 01:20:56,726
CHILDREN'S DOCUMENTS

1505
01:20:58,019 --> 01:20:59,980
This is what I need.

1506
01:21:08,280 --> 01:21:10,365
-Hi, Beth.
-<i>Hi, Mr. Fred.</i>

1507
01:21:10,448 --> 01:21:13,994
Listen, the board scheduled a meeting
for 5:00 p.m. today.

1508
01:21:14,077 --> 01:21:15,662
But how? I'm on leave.

1509
01:21:15,745 --> 01:21:18,456
They know you're on leave, Mr. Fred,

1510
01:21:18,540 --> 01:21:21,084
but they said it's urgent, okay?

1511
01:21:21,167 --> 01:21:23,044
Oh my God. Anything else, Beth?

1512
01:21:23,628 --> 01:21:26,172
If you have a rose quartz,

1513
01:21:26,256 --> 01:21:30,302
a Saint George medallion,
a lucky charm, bring it.

1514
01:21:30,385 --> 01:21:32,137
All right. Thank you, Beth.

1515
01:21:32,220 --> 01:21:33,346
You're welcome.

1516
01:21:37,517 --> 01:21:39,060
Okay. I know it's here.

1517
01:21:43,315 --> 01:21:44,566
Oh, honey.

1518
01:21:48,069 --> 01:21:49,321
So beautiful.

1519
01:21:51,156 --> 01:21:52,324
Damn.

1520
01:21:53,033 --> 01:21:55,243
Here it is.

1521
01:21:56,745 --> 01:21:57,704
Let's see.

1522
01:21:59,664 --> 01:22:00,582
What?

1523
01:22:00,665 --> 01:22:02,042
BIRTH CERTIFICATE: MALU GUIMARÃES

1524
01:22:02,125 --> 01:22:03,209
It says 9 p.m.

1525
01:22:05,420 --> 01:22:06,463
I knew it.

1526
01:22:07,714 --> 01:22:09,591
I mean, I didn't know that I knew…

1527
01:22:11,635 --> 01:22:12,886
but I knew.

1528
01:22:14,721 --> 01:22:16,389
I knew it, honey.

1529
01:22:19,100 --> 01:22:20,352
Damn.

1530
01:22:21,561 --> 01:22:24,064
My punctual girl, Daddy knew it, sweetie.

1531
01:22:29,402 --> 01:22:31,655
If this had been earlier,
he'd be at daycare.

1532
01:22:31,738 --> 01:22:35,867
Since you scheduled the meeting for later,
he's here, but it's all under control.

1533
01:22:35,951 --> 01:22:38,453
It's a rabbit, son. Thank you, by the way.

1534
01:22:38,536 --> 01:22:40,080
Well, gentlemen.

1535
01:22:40,747 --> 01:22:44,417
As you all know,
I'll be stepping away from the company,

1536
01:22:44,501 --> 01:22:47,128
and I'd like to announce
the new General Manager.

1537
01:22:47,212 --> 01:22:51,549
From now on, you'll officially report

1538
01:22:52,300 --> 01:22:53,593
to Dante.

1539
01:23:03,269 --> 01:23:04,813
As for you, Fred,

1540
01:23:04,896 --> 01:23:09,859
given the recent unfortunate events,

1541
01:23:09,943 --> 01:23:13,113
it's no longer appropriate
for you to remain Head of HR.

1542
01:23:13,697 --> 01:23:15,865
The Board has agreed

1543
01:23:15,949 --> 01:23:20,704
to move you
to the Institutional Relations Department.

1544
01:23:20,787 --> 01:23:21,913
-That's it.
-Daddy.

1545
01:23:23,498 --> 01:23:24,541
What did you say, son?

1546
01:23:25,375 --> 01:23:26,793
Fred, are you serious?

1547
01:23:27,377 --> 01:23:28,753
Did you say "Daddy"?

1548
01:23:30,005 --> 01:23:32,257
-Daddy.
-Daddy. He said "Daddy."

1549
01:23:32,340 --> 01:23:33,341
Have you lost--

1550
01:23:33,425 --> 01:23:35,885
Have you lost all respect? I'm speaking.

1551
01:23:38,346 --> 01:23:39,639
No, I haven't, Mr. Pontes.

1552
01:23:39,723 --> 01:23:42,809
I completely understand why
you'd want to keep me at the company.

1553
01:23:42,892 --> 01:23:44,811
I know I'm an excellent professional.

1554
01:23:44,894 --> 01:23:48,314
But at the moment,
it makes no sense for me to be here.

1555
01:23:49,274 --> 01:23:52,235
It doesn't. So, as the Head of HR,

1556
01:23:52,861 --> 01:23:57,032
I fire myself and, as an employee,
I accept my resignation.

1557
01:24:00,076 --> 01:24:03,538
I'll come by later and get
everything sorted out, severance and all.

1558
01:24:03,621 --> 01:24:05,165
But for now,

1559
01:24:05,248 --> 01:24:06,750
we're out of here.

1560
01:24:06,833 --> 01:24:08,960
We're leaving, right, Tom Tom?

1561
01:24:09,044 --> 01:24:13,840
We're going home to draw and be happy,
because I love you, sweetie.

1562
01:24:13,923 --> 01:24:16,885
Congratulations to all of you.
Let me grab my things.

1563
01:24:16,968 --> 01:24:18,386
Say "bye" to everyone.

1564
01:24:18,470 --> 01:24:19,971
Bye, everyone.

1565
01:24:20,055 --> 01:24:21,056
Bye.

1566
01:24:21,139 --> 01:24:22,974
We're very happy. Bye.

1567
01:24:24,017 --> 01:24:26,061
"Daddy." He said "Daddy."

1568
01:24:27,479 --> 01:24:28,897
He said "Daddy."

1569
01:24:33,735 --> 01:24:37,530
Oh, Mr. Fred, I'll miss you.

1570
01:24:37,614 --> 01:24:38,531
Really?

1571
01:24:38,615 --> 01:24:42,702
Really, Mr. Fred. I have a psychiatrist
who prescribes some strong medication.

1572
01:24:42,786 --> 01:24:44,829
Rose quartz is nice, you know?

1573
01:24:44,913 --> 01:24:47,874
But sometimes prescription meds
are what do the trick.

1574
01:24:47,957 --> 01:24:48,958
I'm fine. We're fine.

1575
01:24:49,042 --> 01:24:51,961
Bye, Beth. We're fine and happy,
all right?

1576
01:24:52,045 --> 01:24:54,047
Right? We're great, Beth.

1577
01:24:54,130 --> 01:24:55,715
We are great, aren't we?

1578
01:24:56,216 --> 01:24:57,592
We're wonderful.

1579
01:25:10,980 --> 01:25:12,065
It's here.

1580
01:25:21,825 --> 01:25:24,410
Mr. Fred, what are you doing here?

1581
01:25:24,494 --> 01:25:26,412
I look a mess.

1582
01:25:27,163 --> 01:25:28,581
Tom Tom!

1583
01:25:32,043 --> 01:25:35,171
Mr. Fred, this girl has worked
in so many places

1584
01:25:35,255 --> 01:25:38,049
I didn't even know
the last one was your company.

1585
01:25:38,758 --> 01:25:42,679
I'm sorry about Brenda.
I'm so embarrassed I wish I could hide.

1586
01:25:42,762 --> 01:25:45,807
Listen, I'm the one
who needs to apologize, okay?

1587
01:25:46,558 --> 01:25:48,977
-Is Brenda here?
-Yeah, she's upstairs.

1588
01:25:49,060 --> 01:25:51,312
-I'll go talk to her.
-Go on.

1589
01:25:51,396 --> 01:25:53,314
I'll stay here with Tom Tom.

1590
01:25:53,398 --> 01:25:55,191
Right, sweetie?

1591
01:26:00,738 --> 01:26:01,948
What are you doing here?

1592
01:26:02,031 --> 01:26:05,535
I came to give you a gift
and apologize, because…

1593
01:26:05,618 --> 01:26:07,245
-Did you buy that for me?
-No.

1594
01:26:07,328 --> 01:26:10,832
I mean, it is for you, but this one I…

1595
01:26:12,333 --> 01:26:14,252
-What?
-I stole it.

1596
01:26:14,335 --> 01:26:16,796
-No way.
-It's true.

1597
01:26:16,880 --> 01:26:20,091
And you're absolutely right,
that place is awful.

1598
01:26:20,175 --> 01:26:21,509
I was awful,

1599
01:26:21,593 --> 01:26:24,596
but that place has a way
of making us all more and more awful.

1600
01:26:24,679 --> 01:26:25,680
I'm sorry, okay?

1601
01:26:25,763 --> 01:26:29,267
And I can get you another job,
in a better place.

1602
01:26:30,435 --> 01:26:31,603
Thank you, then.

1603
01:26:31,686 --> 01:26:33,938
Once I get my life in order, because…

1604
01:26:35,106 --> 01:26:36,649
I quit too.

1605
01:26:37,150 --> 01:26:38,443
-You quit?
-Mm-hmm.

1606
01:26:38,526 --> 01:26:39,694
-No way.
-Yes.

1607
01:26:39,777 --> 01:26:41,112
-For real?
-For real.

1608
01:26:41,988 --> 01:26:43,489
Do you see that thing over there?

1609
01:26:43,573 --> 01:26:45,074
-Yes.
-It's half assembled.

1610
01:26:45,158 --> 01:26:48,745
There. It's a piece of furniture
I bought for Aunt Simone.

1611
01:26:48,828 --> 01:26:51,706
She wanted something for the living room.
So I gave it to her.

1612
01:26:51,789 --> 01:26:55,043
I bought it in 78 installments,
I didn't know I'd get fired.

1613
01:26:55,126 --> 01:26:58,046
I ordered it unassembled
because assembled was more expensive.

1614
01:26:58,129 --> 01:27:00,924
It arrived with three screws missing.
Where did I buy it?

1615
01:27:01,007 --> 01:27:02,550
-Rabbit Home Center.
-No.

1616
01:27:02,634 --> 01:27:06,262
-But we can fix that now.
-Let's do it.

1617
01:27:06,346 --> 01:27:07,680
There you go.

1618
01:27:09,766 --> 01:27:10,767
Thank you.

1619
01:27:10,850 --> 01:27:12,268
I heard about Family Day.

1620
01:27:14,604 --> 01:27:17,398
-I'm sorry, okay? I overdid it.
-No problem at all.

1621
01:27:17,482 --> 01:27:20,777
I mean, none of my organs are
where they're supposed to be anymore.

1622
01:27:20,860 --> 01:27:24,322
The farm's been devastated,
but everything's under control.

1623
01:27:24,405 --> 01:27:26,324
But I know I was being very selfish.

1624
01:27:26,407 --> 01:27:28,159
-Yeah.
-So Roberta has every right

1625
01:27:28,243 --> 01:27:29,327
to be upset with me.

1626
01:27:29,410 --> 01:27:30,370
Mm-hmm.

1627
01:27:31,037 --> 01:27:33,373
And my kids have every right
not to like me anymore.

1628
01:27:33,456 --> 01:27:35,458
No, stop it. Of course they like you.

1629
01:27:35,541 --> 01:27:36,960
Your kids are really cool.

1630
01:27:37,043 --> 01:27:39,671
They wouldn't be so cool
if you weren't too.

1631
01:27:41,005 --> 01:27:42,715
It's done. It looks good.

1632
01:27:45,760 --> 01:27:47,011
You're good.

1633
01:27:52,809 --> 01:27:54,102
Your kids like you.

1634
01:27:55,353 --> 01:27:57,563
But they're not even talking to me.

1635
01:27:57,647 --> 01:27:59,857
But it must be hard for them, right?

1636
01:27:59,941 --> 01:28:02,610
Knowing they hurt you
with that Family Day prank.

1637
01:28:02,694 --> 01:28:05,029
Talk to them, man. You're their father.

1638
01:28:05,530 --> 01:28:08,032
Am I still?

1639
01:28:10,785 --> 01:28:12,370
It has a translation, you know?

1640
01:28:12,453 --> 01:28:14,330
In Portuguese, it's <i>Dia da Família.</i>

1641
01:28:14,414 --> 01:28:16,249
How the tables have turned.

1642
01:28:16,332 --> 01:28:17,500
I'm a fast learner.

1643
01:28:18,293 --> 01:28:19,127
Give me a hug.

1644
01:28:19,210 --> 01:28:21,671
You're lucky I'm not a Scorpio.

1645
01:28:21,754 --> 01:28:24,340
-Thanks. And what are you?
-I don't hold grudges.

1646
01:28:24,424 --> 01:28:25,842
-I'm a Taurus.
-Like Tom Tom.

1647
01:28:25,925 --> 01:28:27,719
-Tom Tom is a Taurus?
-You didn't know?

1648
01:28:27,802 --> 01:28:30,471
-I didn't.
-Why do you think he eats so much?

1649
01:28:30,555 --> 01:28:33,891
-Maybe he has worms?
-No, he eats fruits, rice, beans…

1650
01:28:38,396 --> 01:28:40,481
Brand-new diaper, right? Yay!

1651
01:28:41,316 --> 01:28:43,359
-Score!
-Yeah!

1652
01:28:43,443 --> 01:28:46,529
-Rest.
-Yeah! That's it.

1653
01:28:46,612 --> 01:28:49,324
That's it, girl!
She's got nothing on the left!

1654
01:28:49,407 --> 01:28:52,076
Nothing on the left! Hit it left!

1655
01:28:52,160 --> 01:28:54,829
Okay? Focus, relax, breathe.

1656
01:28:54,912 --> 01:28:57,415
Hit her left side. Focus, okay?

1657
01:28:57,498 --> 01:28:58,791
-Are you listening?
-Yeah.

1658
01:28:58,875 --> 01:29:01,252
-Go, hit her left side.
-Okay, Dad.

1659
01:29:03,212 --> 01:29:06,132
Son, I can't believe
you were studying anatomy

1660
01:29:06,215 --> 01:29:07,633
with my best friend's daughter.

1661
01:29:07,717 --> 01:29:09,510
She's practically your cousin.

1662
01:29:09,594 --> 01:29:11,971
You're offended.
That's all you have to say?

1663
01:29:12,055 --> 01:29:16,184
I'm not offended, I'm a survivor.
I didn't put my kids in a giant ball.

1664
01:29:16,267 --> 01:29:18,019
I survived by some miracle.

1665
01:29:18,102 --> 01:29:19,854
-Score!
-Some miracle!

1666
01:29:21,856 --> 01:29:25,860
Us surviving with you
taking care of us was also a miracle, Dad.

1667
01:29:25,943 --> 01:29:27,278
Jesus, honey.

1668
01:29:29,864 --> 01:29:31,074
I'm sorry.

1669
01:29:32,200 --> 01:29:33,701
I'm sorry too, Dad.

1670
01:29:35,161 --> 01:29:35,995
Okay.

1671
01:29:37,038 --> 01:29:39,374
Yeah, Dad. I'm sorry.

1672
01:29:41,125 --> 01:29:42,919
I'm sorry, Dad.

1673
01:29:45,129 --> 01:29:46,464
I'm sorry, guys.

1674
01:29:46,547 --> 01:29:47,715
It was my bad.

1675
01:29:47,799 --> 01:29:50,802
Maybe you could save
family therapy for another time.

1676
01:29:50,885 --> 01:29:52,261
Just a second.

1677
01:29:52,345 --> 01:29:54,013
Another time that never comes.

1678
01:29:54,097 --> 01:29:56,808
If he's anything like you,
it will never be the right time.

1679
01:29:56,891 --> 01:29:58,017
What the hell, Júlia?

1680
01:29:58,101 --> 01:30:00,978
Disrespecting your mother
just because you have an audience?

1681
01:30:01,062 --> 01:30:03,856
When we get home, we'll chat. Don't worry.

1682
01:30:03,940 --> 01:30:07,026
No. When we get home,
you'll be on your phone.

1683
01:30:07,110 --> 01:30:08,403
See what I mean?

1684
01:30:08,486 --> 01:30:10,947
It's so sad to see a family fighting.

1685
01:30:11,030 --> 01:30:13,366
They're fighting,
but at least they're talking.

1686
01:30:13,449 --> 01:30:15,243
You don't talk or fight.

1687
01:30:15,326 --> 01:30:17,662
You never even asked
if I like these games.

1688
01:30:17,745 --> 01:30:19,956
-What do you mean, son?
-Quiet down, everyone.

1689
01:30:20,039 --> 01:30:22,083
-You're disturbing the game!
-That's right.

1690
01:30:22,166 --> 01:30:25,336
You're the referee,
not a family court judge, okay?

1691
01:30:25,837 --> 01:30:27,922
Hey!

1692
01:30:28,005 --> 01:30:29,882
-The man asked for silence!
-Yes.

1693
01:30:29,966 --> 01:30:33,094
Anyone who's not interested
in the tennis match is free to leave.

1694
01:30:33,177 --> 01:30:35,346
-Me!
-What?

1695
01:30:35,430 --> 01:30:39,016
I'm exhausted from practicing every day
and getting up early to do it.

1696
01:30:39,100 --> 01:30:40,852
I don't even like tennis.

1697
01:30:40,935 --> 01:30:42,687
I do it because you bug me.

1698
01:30:42,770 --> 01:30:43,896
But, honey…

1699
01:30:43,980 --> 01:30:46,149
Also because I know it's important to you.

1700
01:30:46,232 --> 01:30:47,442
But, honey…

1701
01:30:48,609 --> 01:30:50,278
Oh, for crying out loud.

1702
01:30:50,361 --> 01:30:52,947
I didn't even want to come,
and we won't have a match?

1703
01:30:53,030 --> 01:30:55,199
Hey, lady, do you mind?

1704
01:30:55,283 --> 01:30:57,702
-Go fu--
-Hey! Calm down.

1705
01:30:57,785 --> 01:30:59,745
Look at the example we're setting here.

1706
01:30:59,829 --> 01:31:02,123
Really? You're talking
about setting an example?

1707
01:31:02,206 --> 01:31:05,209
-What do you mean by that, son?
-You don't pay attention to me…

1708
01:31:05,293 --> 01:31:07,378
We came to see my friend.

1709
01:31:07,462 --> 01:31:09,755
These annoying people
are bothering my daughter.

1710
01:31:09,839 --> 01:31:11,340
Wait, guys.

1711
01:31:11,424 --> 01:31:12,550
Just a second.

1712
01:31:12,633 --> 01:31:15,011
Relax, you're nervous.
That's normal, honey.

1713
01:31:15,094 --> 01:31:16,512
There's no need for that.

1714
01:31:16,596 --> 01:31:18,514
Guys, team, gather up.

1715
01:31:18,598 --> 01:31:20,391
It's the perfect time for us to leave.

1716
01:31:20,475 --> 01:31:21,726
-Let's go?
-Let's go.

1717
01:31:21,809 --> 01:31:22,810
Come on, son.

1718
01:31:23,853 --> 01:31:26,814
Come here, honey. Let's play.

1719
01:31:26,898 --> 01:31:27,815
You're amazing!

1720
01:31:27,899 --> 01:31:29,984
Playing… It's all right.

1721
01:31:30,067 --> 01:31:33,654
Let's go. We'll be happier
once we're out of this madness.

1722
01:31:39,035 --> 01:31:42,872
Look, my little crew, my loves,
I know you're upset,

1723
01:31:42,955 --> 01:31:46,000
with those grumpy faces,
but the universe just showed us

1724
01:31:46,083 --> 01:31:48,461
a spectacular example
of a dysfunctional family.

1725
01:31:48,544 --> 01:31:50,087
So, it could be much worse.

1726
01:31:50,171 --> 01:31:53,799
So, Dad may be doing poorly,
but it could be much worse.

1727
01:31:57,803 --> 01:32:01,182
Now… No. Now I want to see
everyone helping me clean up this mess.

1728
01:32:01,265 --> 01:32:03,100
-No.
-Guys!

1729
01:32:03,184 --> 01:32:05,311
-Tom Tom.
-Tom Tom is going to…

1730
01:32:05,394 --> 01:32:08,856
-Tom Tom!
-Tom Tom!

1731
01:32:26,040 --> 01:32:28,209
Look who's here!

1732
01:32:28,292 --> 01:32:29,126
Huh?

1733
01:32:32,964 --> 01:32:35,341
-Mom? Weren't you coming tomorrow?
-My son!

1734
01:32:35,424 --> 01:32:38,970
-Mommy's back. Squeeze Mommy.
-I missed you, Mom!

1735
01:32:39,720 --> 01:32:40,763
I missed you.

1736
01:32:40,846 --> 01:32:42,640
You look beautiful, Mom.

1737
01:32:46,435 --> 01:32:48,896
-Look who's here.
-Look who's here.

1738
01:32:48,980 --> 01:32:50,481
-You're here!
-You're here!

1739
01:32:52,733 --> 01:32:54,819
-You're here!
-She's here.

1740
01:32:54,902 --> 01:32:57,321
She's here!

1741
01:32:57,405 --> 01:33:00,700
-Mommy's here.
-I missed you so much!

1742
01:33:00,783 --> 01:33:02,994
Oh, God. Jesus Christ.

1743
01:33:03,077 --> 01:33:05,663
Hey, team, he pooped.

1744
01:33:05,746 --> 01:33:09,417
-It's my turn to change him.
-No, let me!

1745
01:33:09,500 --> 01:33:10,668
Yeah?

1746
01:33:11,586 --> 01:33:14,297
-Yeah.
-I'm gonna watch them, okay, Mom?

1747
01:33:14,380 --> 01:33:18,426
And I'll also put your things away.
You must be tired from the trip.

1748
01:33:18,509 --> 01:33:20,177
-Kisses.
-Kisses. Bye.

1749
01:33:21,429 --> 01:33:23,306
-Wonderful.
-What did you do with my kids?

1750
01:33:23,389 --> 01:33:25,141
-Huh?
-Did you drug them?

1751
01:33:25,224 --> 01:33:27,310
-No!
-My children, Fred.

1752
01:33:27,935 --> 01:33:30,563
-How are you? I missed you so much.
-You look beautiful.

1753
01:33:30,646 --> 01:33:31,856
My God.

1754
01:33:31,939 --> 01:33:33,899
-Were you desperate?
-No.

1755
01:33:33,983 --> 01:33:37,069
-Felt like curling up and crying?
-No.

1756
01:33:37,153 --> 01:33:39,447
No? You didn't age
a hundred years in one day?

1757
01:33:39,530 --> 01:33:42,491
I aged a little. But it's okay,
you're back and you're beautiful.

1758
01:33:42,575 --> 01:33:44,952
I need to tell you
something very important.

1759
01:33:45,036 --> 01:33:47,204
-Me too.
-Are you serious? For the love of God.

1760
01:33:47,288 --> 01:33:49,415
You're back
with something important to tell me.

1761
01:33:49,498 --> 01:33:50,541
You go first.

1762
01:33:50,625 --> 01:33:54,253
Honey, I don't want to be
a full-time mom and housewife.

1763
01:33:54,337 --> 01:33:56,505
I need to be happy. I need to…

1764
01:33:57,131 --> 01:33:59,550
For the sake of our family,
I'm going back to work.

1765
01:33:59,634 --> 01:34:00,551
Are you serious?

1766
01:34:01,344 --> 01:34:03,262
And I quit my job, honey.

1767
01:34:03,346 --> 01:34:05,514
-No way.
-I quit my job.

1768
01:34:05,598 --> 01:34:07,308
-Really?
-Really.

1769
01:34:07,391 --> 01:34:10,436
-But now what?
-Now you'll be the breadwinner.

1770
01:34:11,354 --> 01:34:12,521
I'll take care of things.

1771
01:34:12,605 --> 01:34:15,608
It will be wonderful, we're a team.
And you're back, and beautiful.

1772
01:34:15,691 --> 01:34:19,737
-I love you.
-I love you. I missed you so much.

1773
01:34:19,820 --> 01:34:20,655
Oh my God.

1774
01:34:20,738 --> 01:34:21,572
Ew!

1775
01:34:21,656 --> 01:34:25,201
-Oh, hi!
-Mom, we found out Dad's terrible.

1776
01:34:25,284 --> 01:34:26,869
But at least he tries.

1777
01:34:26,952 --> 01:34:29,830
And we missed you so much.

1778
01:34:30,706 --> 01:34:32,792
But we're happy you look beautiful.

1779
01:34:32,875 --> 01:34:35,711
-What's it like there?
-Salvador is so beautiful.

1780
01:34:35,795 --> 01:34:37,880
It's so nice. I've already decided.

1781
01:34:37,963 --> 01:34:41,217
At least once a year,
I'll spend ten days there.

1782
01:34:41,300 --> 01:34:43,386
Wait. Gather up, guys, team meeting.

1783
01:34:43,469 --> 01:34:46,180
Let's decide if we'll let Mom
keep going to Salvador.

1784
01:34:46,263 --> 01:34:48,140
What's this attachment to Salvador?

1785
01:34:48,224 --> 01:34:49,642
Guys, it's magical.

1786
01:34:50,643 --> 01:34:53,854
-There's an energy, a glow.
-Turn that glow down a bit.

1787
01:34:53,938 --> 01:34:56,691
No, keep your beautiful glow,
but here with us. We need you.

1788
01:34:56,774 --> 01:34:58,859
I know all the dance routines, okay?

1789
01:34:58,943 --> 01:35:01,737
Mom's the new redhead from É o Tchan now.

1790
01:35:01,821 --> 01:35:04,907
-What is É o Tchan, Mom?
-No way, João!

1791
01:35:04,990 --> 01:35:07,159
-I'll play it now.
-It's an axé band.

1792
01:35:07,243 --> 01:35:09,870
-Come on, shake it.
-No. I learned how to change diapers.

1793
01:35:09,954 --> 01:35:11,831
-Yeah.
-To get kids settled into daycare.

1794
01:35:11,914 --> 01:35:13,874
Now I have to learn É o Tchan dance moves?

1795
01:35:13,958 --> 01:35:15,209
Loosen up. You can do it.

1796
01:35:15,292 --> 01:35:17,628
-Just a second, Beta.
-Come on!

1797
01:35:17,712 --> 01:35:19,797
-Yes, Malu!
-Come here, Clacla.

1798
01:35:19,880 --> 01:35:21,882
Help your sister. We have to go under it.

1799
01:35:21,966 --> 01:35:24,552
-I can't do that.
-Higher, for the love of God.

1800
01:35:24,635 --> 01:35:26,470
My back. Come on!

1801
01:35:27,555 --> 01:35:28,723
Jesus Christ!

1802
01:35:30,558 --> 01:35:32,601
This is such a good song!

1803
01:35:35,980 --> 01:35:38,023
-Here! Hey!
-Yeah.

1804
01:35:41,861 --> 01:35:44,280
-Jump!
-Come on, move it.

1805
01:36:10,598 --> 01:36:16,687
DADDY'S IN TROUBLE

1806
01:36:20,691 --> 01:36:24,737
<i>Fred, you're not going to believe this.</i>
<i>Did Beth tell you?</i>

1807
01:36:24,820 --> 01:36:27,823
<i>Dante's wife heard</i>
<i>about Roberta's arrangement</i>

1808
01:36:27,907 --> 01:36:30,534
<i>and took off for Miami,</i>
<i>leaving the kids with him.</i>

1809
01:36:30,618 --> 01:36:32,578
<i>Don't even know when she's coming back.</i>

1810
01:36:33,120 --> 01:36:35,372
<i>Matheus, what a juicy piece of gossip!</i>

1811
01:36:35,456 --> 01:36:37,458
<i>The best I get is school gossip here.</i>

1812
01:36:37,541 --> 01:36:39,168
<i>I need some grown-up gossip.</i>

1813
01:36:39,251 --> 01:36:41,128
<i>So you're saying Dante is…</i>

1814
01:36:42,379 --> 01:36:44,173
<i>The guy's emasculated.</i>

1815
01:36:44,256 --> 01:36:48,803
<i>He shows up for work with the same outfit</i>
<i>every day, like a cartoon character.</i>

1816
01:36:49,678 --> 01:36:53,474
<i>Everyone's saying Pontes was</i>
<i>the one holding everything together.</i>

1817
01:36:54,183 --> 01:36:57,561
<i>Oh! Wasn't he "the best in Cambridge"?</i>

1818
01:36:57,645 --> 01:36:59,313
<i>With his perfect family?</i>

1819
01:37:00,648 --> 01:37:03,192
<i>Even Tom Tom is laughing.</i>
<i>Aren't you, buddy?</i>

1820
01:37:03,776 --> 01:37:07,279
<i>He asked for your number.</i>
<i>Wanted to know if you were still idle.</i>

1821
01:37:07,363 --> 01:37:11,534
<i>Idle? What do you mean, Matheus?</i>
<i>I was idle at Rabbit Home Center.</i>

1822
01:37:11,617 --> 01:37:14,995
<i>Here at home, I'm doing lambaerobics,</i>
<i>fit dance, CrossFit,</i>

1823
01:37:15,079 --> 01:37:18,207
<i>but not lifting gym weights.</i>
<i>I'm lifting kids' backpacks.</i>

1824
01:37:18,290 --> 01:37:21,710
<i>Hey, he just sent me a message!</i>
<i>Hold on, let me listen!</i>

1825
01:37:21,794 --> 01:37:26,257
<i>Yo, Fred! Long time no see.</i>
<i>How are you, my friend? It's Dante.</i>

1826
01:37:26,340 --> 01:37:29,468
<i>You know we'll welcome you back</i>
<i>whenever you want.</i>

1827
01:37:29,552 --> 01:37:32,513
<i>Rabbit Home Center's your family.</i>
<i>I guarantee a great salary.</i>

1828
01:37:32,596 --> 01:37:35,850
<i>Name your price, all right?</i>
<i>Are you interested? Oh!</i>

1829
01:37:35,933 --> 01:37:38,102
<i>Call me back. I'm waiting.</i>
<i>Don't forget about me, Fred.</i>

1830
01:37:38,185 --> 01:37:39,395
{\an8}HONEY! BETINHA! LISTEN TO THIS!

1831
01:37:39,478 --> 01:37:40,896
<i>Is that Dante? Jesus!</i>

1832
01:37:40,980 --> 01:37:42,523
YEAH!!!!

1833
01:37:42,606 --> 01:37:44,400
<i>Wait until he finds out</i>

1834
01:37:44,483 --> 01:37:49,238
<i>that the lawyer helping Brenda</i>
<i>sue Rabbit Home Center is me.</i>

1835
01:37:49,321 --> 01:37:50,781
<i>He's going to freak out!</i>

1836
01:37:52,783 --> 01:37:56,745
<i>Honey, can you send me some pictures</i>
<i>of the kids? I miss them.</i>

1837
01:37:56,829 --> 01:37:57,872
<i>Okay, I'll send them.</i>

1838
01:37:57,955 --> 01:38:00,875
<i>But as soon as you see the mess</i>
<i>they're making around the house,</i>

1839
01:38:00,958 --> 01:38:02,459
<i>you'll stop missing them.</i>

1840
01:38:03,335 --> 01:38:06,922
<i>Mr. Fred, I love working</i>
<i>at Mrs. Roberta's office.</i>

1841
01:38:07,006 --> 01:38:10,259
<i>Who knew? The worst thing</i>
<i>to ever happen to me, you,</i>

1842
01:38:10,342 --> 01:38:13,762
<i>led to the best thing</i>
<i>to ever happen to me, Mrs. Roberta.</i>

1843
01:38:13,846 --> 01:38:16,140
<i>This woman is not a lawyer, Mr. Fred.</i>

1844
01:38:16,223 --> 01:38:19,351
<i>She's a dragon tamer.</i>
<i>You should see what she does around here.</i>

1845
01:38:19,435 --> 01:38:21,812
<i>She'll destroy that bastard Dante.</i>

1846
01:38:21,896 --> 01:38:24,565
<i>She'll make him cry screw tears.</i>
<i>You'll see.</i>

1847
01:38:25,774 --> 01:38:27,192
<i>What the hell is this?</i>

1848
01:38:27,276 --> 01:38:31,780
<i>-Did you like it? The kids made it.</i>
-<i>I thought so. I could tell right away.</i>

1849
01:38:31,864 --> 01:38:34,700
<i>I would never expect</i>
<i>such creativity from you.</i>

1850
01:38:34,783 --> 01:38:36,619
<i>With all due respect, Mr. Fred.</i>

1851
01:38:41,373 --> 01:38:43,375
MATHEUS
I JUST HEARD! DANTE IS DES…

1852
01:38:44,335 --> 01:38:46,921
<i>Matheus, he's desperate.</i>

1853
01:38:47,004 --> 01:38:51,300
<i>Should I let him know I'm not coming back,</i>
<i>or let him suffer for a while?</i>

1854
01:38:51,383 --> 01:38:52,927
<i>Dad, Clarice's hitting me.</i>

1855
01:38:53,010 --> 01:38:57,681
<i>Clacla, stop! João, you're the oldest.</i>
<i>Set an example. God! Where are you going?</i>

1856
01:38:57,765 --> 01:39:00,100
<i>-Who's outside?</i>
<i>-No one, Dad. A friend.</i>

1857
01:39:00,184 --> 01:39:03,562
<i>Look, when your mom gets here,</i>
<i>we're going to have a talk.</i>

1858
01:39:03,646 --> 01:39:06,607
<i>It's Double Tuesday.</i>
<i>She's going to the bar with Brenda.</i>

1859
01:39:06,690 --> 01:39:08,943
<i>Did you hear that, Matheus? Hold on.</i>

1860
01:39:09,026 --> 01:39:12,571
<i>Roberta, I'll need ten days in Salvador.</i>
<i>Okay? In the summer!</i>

1861
01:39:13,489 --> 01:39:15,991
<i>-I want to go too.</i>
<i>-Figure it out, Betinha!</i>

1862
01:39:17,242 --> 01:39:18,786
<i>Timbalada!</i>

1863
01:42:07,663 --> 01:42:12,668
Subtitle translation by: J. Jones